{"id": "civic_digitalindiagovin_18aa84b4_01", "source_url": "https://www.digitalindia.gov.in/photo_gallery/union-minister-ashwini-vaishnaw-launches-guidelines-and-portal-for-electronics-component-manufacturing-scheme/", "title": "Digital India Official Portal - Union Minister Ashwini Vaishnaw Launches Guidelines and Portal for Electronics Component Manufacturing Scheme 15+", "section": "Overview", "text": "Union Minister Ashwini Vaishnaw Launches Guidelines and Portal for Electronics Component Manufacturing Scheme Union Minister for Electronics and Information Technology Shri Ashwini Vaishnaw launched the guidelines and portal on 26 April 2025, for the Electronics Component Manufacturing Scheme (ECMS), marking a major step towards strengthening India’s electronics manufacturing ecosystem. The initiative aims to bolster domestic production of electronic components across sectors like telecommunications, automotive, and energy, while creating approximately 92,000 direct jobs. The scheme includes employment-linked incentives to attract manufacturers and strengthen India’s electronics supply chain.", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["digitalindiagovin", "guideline", "info", "portal", "scheme"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_digitalindiagovin_7dc6758f_01", "source_url": "https://www.digitalindia.gov.in/photo_gallery/digital-india-talk-show-organised-at-nerist-arunachal-pradesh-to-promote-digital-literacy-and-citizen-centric-digital-services/", "title": "Digital India Official Portal - Digital India Talk Show organised at NERIST, Arunachal Pradesh to promote Digital Literacy and Citizen-Centric Digital Services 11+", "section": "Overview", "text": "Digital India Talk Show organised at NERIST, Arunachal Pradesh to promote Digital Literacy and Citizen-Centric Digital Services As part of its continued outreach activities, the National e-Governance Division (NeGD), Ministry of Electronics & Information Technology (MeitY), Government of India, in collaboration with the North Eastern Regional Institute of Science and Technology (NERIST) and the Institution of Engineers (India) (IEI), Arunachal Pradesh State Centre, organised a Digital India Talk Show cum Interactive Workshop at the NERIST Seminar Hall, Department of Computer Science & Engineering, on June 19, 2026. The workshop aimed at creating awareness about the Government of India’s flagship Digital India initiatives, promote digital literacy, and familiarise participants with citizen-centric digital services and emerging technologies that are transforming governance and public service delivery.", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["about", "citizen", "digitalindiagovin", "info", "service"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_digitalindiagovin_d8740b6f_01", "source_url": "https://www.digitalindia.gov.in/photo_gallery/inauguration-of-the-myscheme-portal-in-uttarakhand-a-step-towards-digital-governance/", "title": "Digital India Official Portal - Inauguration of the myScheme Portal in Uttarakhand: A Step Towards Digital Governance 16+", "section": "Overview", "text": "Inauguration of the myScheme Portal in Uttarakhand: A Step Towards Digital Governance The myScheme Portal was inaugurated on December 10, 2025, in Dehradun, Uttarakhand, by the Hon’ble Chief Minister of Uttarakhand, Shri Pushkar Singh Dhami. The inauguration marked an important step in the State’s digital governance initiatives, aimed at strengthening citizen access to government welfare schemes. The myScheme Portal is a unified, user-centric digital platform that enables citizens to easily search, identify, and discover government schemes they are eligible for across multiple sectors. Currently featuring over 400+ state government schemes, the platform is designed to ensure transparency, efficiency, and inclusivity in the delivery of scheme benefits. The event highlighted the Government’s commitment to leveraging technology for last-mile delivery and empowering citizens through simplified access to welfare benefits", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["citizen", "digitalindiagovin", "portal", "scheme"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_digitalindiagovin_1ef0a6cf_01", "source_url": "https://www.digitalindia.gov.in/ask-our-expert/", "title": "Digital India Official Portal - Episode 51 inspires students to lead, serve, and contribute to nation-building through the National Service Scheme (NSS) “The National Service Scheme (NSS) is enabling young people to...", "section": "Overview", "text": "Recent Episode 51 inspires students to lead, serve, and contribute to nation-building through the National Service Scheme (NSS) /?= get_the_title(); ?> Posted on: August 14, 2026 “The National Service Scheme (NSS) is enabling young people to transform community service into opportunities for leadership, skill development and nation-building”, said Shri Ramesh Verma, Director, NSS Division, in the latest episode of Digital India Ask Our Experts, a Digital India initiative of the National e-Governance Division (NeGD), Ministry of Electronics and Information Technology (MeitY), conducted on August 6, 2026. Read More Episode 53 showcases Aqua SURAKSHA, a biosensor developed by C-DAC Kolkata and ICAR-CIFRI /?= get_the_title(); ?> Posted on: October 5, 2026 The 53rd episode of Digital India Ask Our Experts, held on September 1, 2026, showcased Aqua SURAKSHA, a portable, battery-operated biosensor developed by C-DAC Kolkata in collaboration with ICAR-CIFRI to detect organophosphate pesticide residues in water. Read More Episode 54 highlights safety measures before, during and after floods /?= get_the_title(); ?> Posted on: October 5, 2026 Floods can take different forms and their impact can extend well beyond the period when floodwaters recede. The 54th episode of Digital India Ask Our Experts featured Prof. (Dr.) Dinesh Kumar Aswal, National Disaster Management Authority (NDMA), who explained how citizens and communities can prepare for floods, respond to warnings and stay safe from secondary hazards. Read More Episode 55 explores applications of Blockchain in education, e-governance, mobile security and public services /?= get_the_title(); ?> Posted on: October 5, 2026 The latest episode of Digital India Ask Our Experts explores how permissioned Blockchain technology can support more secure, transparent and efficient delivery of government services by strengthening digital trust, data integrity and verification. Read More Episode 52 Addresses Workplace Stress Management and its impact on Health /?= get_the_title(); ?> Posted on: August 28, 2026 The latest episode of Digital India Ask Our Experts, a citizen-centric initiative of the Digital India Programme, Ministry of Electronics & Information Technology (MeitY), was conducted on August 21, 2026, on the topic “Workplace Stress Management”, featuring Dr. Swapan Gupta, Professor of Neurology, G B Pant Hospital, Delhi, in an interactive discussion on workplace stress management and its impact on physical and mental well-being. Read More Episode 48 explores scientific and technology-driven approaches around water management /?= get_the_title(); ?> Posted on: July 13, 2026 The 48th episode of Digital India Ask Our Experts featured an insightful discussion on Protecting Citizens from Floods and Bank Erosion in the Brahmaputra Valley, highlighting the role of science, technology, data-driven planning, and community-focused interventions in managing one of India’s most dynamic river systems. Read More Episode 49 explores how AI and high-performance computing are helping safeguard Sikkim’s Forests from Wildfires /?= get_the_title(); ?> Posted on: July 10, 2026 The 49th episode of Digital India's flagship knowledge series 'Ask Our Experts' showcased how advanced technologies are transforming forest fire management through the Sikkim Wildfire Spread Forecasting", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["citizen", "digitalindiagovin", "help", "info", "scheme", "service"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_wwwmygovin_7b685a81_01", "source_url": "https://www.mygov.in/", "title": "MyGov.in | MyGov: A Platform for Citizen Engagement towards Good Governance in India", "section": "Overview", "text": "The Indian Cybercrime Coordination Centre (I4C), Ministry of Home Affairs, Government of India, in collaboration with MyGov, invites citizens to participate in the Cyber Suraksha Reel Making Competition 2026.The competition aims to encourage citizens to use creativity and digital storytelling to spread awareness about cybercrime, emerging online scams and safe digital practices. Ayushman Bharat Pradhan Mantri Jan Arogya Yojana (AB PM-JAY), launched in 2018, has completed eight years of its journey towards advancing accessible, affordable and quality healthcare for millions of citizens. The scheme provides health cover of up to ₹5 lakh per family per year for secondary and tertiary care hospitalisation and has played a significant role in providing financial protection to eligible families. The Department of Animal Husbandry & Dairying (DAHD), in collaboration with MyGov, is organising a Nationwide Logo Design Competition for “Pashu Aushadhi”. The National Security Guard (NSG) in collaboration with MyGov invite citizens to participate in Poster Making Competition giving them an opportunity to express their appreciation for the courage, sacrifice, dedication and patriotism of the National Security Guard (NSG). Through creative artwork, colours and inspiring messages, participants can showcase the spirit of bravery, discipline and national service and highlight the vital role of NSG personnel in safeguarding the nation. Discover your culture. Tell your story. Share it with India.India’s cultural heritage lives not only in monuments and museums, but also in the stories, traditions, art, music, languages and everyday practices passed down through generations.Through the “My Culture My Story” Contest, MyGov invites citizens to discover and share a unique cultural story from their community, region or heritage. Bureau of Police Research and Development (BPR&D) under Ministry of Home Affairs (MHA) in collaboration with MyGov invites the citizens, especially the youth to participate in the Video Making Contest on Introduction of New Offences in its pursuit to make people more aware of the New Criminal Laws, namely:Bharatiya Nyaya SanhitaBharatiya Nagarik Suraksha SanhitaBharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam The Logistics Division, DPIIT, Ministry of Commerce and Industry, in collaboration with MyGov, invites citizens' suggestions and comments on the National Transport Master Plan, covering connectivity, travel experience and transport priorities for the next 10 years. In an increasingly digital world, cyber safety is everyone’s responsibility. Participate in MyGov’s National Poll Series to assess your awareness of online threats, digital fraud, safe browsing practices, and cybersecurity measures. Share your views and help promote a safer and more secure digital India. The Logistics Division, DPIIT, Ministry of Commerce and Industry, in collaboration with MyGov, invites citizens to take part in this short survey on the 5th Anniversary of the PM GatiShakti National Master Plan. PM GatiShakti is an integrated platform for planning of roads, railways, airports, ports, waterways and other infrastructure with ‘Whole of Area’ and ‘Whole of Government’ approach, for seamless, multi-modal connectivity and smoother movement of people and goods. Project Veer Gatha was instituted under Gallantry Awards Portal (GAP) in", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["about", "citizen", "help", "portal", "scheme", "service", "wwwmygovin"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_wwwmygovin_511d62b3_01", "source_url": "https://www.mygov.in/overview", "title": "MyGov: An Overview | MyGov", "section": "Overview", "text": "The citizen-centric platform empowers people to connect with the Government & contribute towards good governance. MyGov has been established as Government of India’s Citizen Engagement Platform which collaborates with multiple Government bodies/ Ministries to engage with citizens for policy formulation and seeks the opinion of people on issues/ topics of public interest and welfare. Since its launch on 26th July 2014, MyGov has 64.60 million registered users as on 1 September 2026. Almost all Government Departments leverage MyGov platform for their citizen engagement activities, consultations for policy formulation and also to disseminate information to citizens for various Government schemes and programs. MyGov is amongst the most active profiles on Social Media – Twitter, Facebook, Instagram, YouTube & LinkedIn with the username @MyGovIndia. MyGov has a significant presence on several Indian social media platforms like Koo, Sharechat, Chingari, Roposo, Bolo Indya and Mitron. MyGov has adopted multiple engagement methodologies like discussions, tasks, polls, surveys, blogs, talks, pledges, quizzes and on-ground activities by innovatively using internet, mobile apps, IVRS, SMS and outbound dialling (OBD) technologies. MyGov has also launched State instances in 28 States/UTs, namely Himachal Pradesh, Haryana, Maharashtra, Madhya Pradesh, Arunachal Pradesh, Assam, Manipur, Tripura, Chhattisgarh, Jharkhand, Nagaland, Uttarakhand, Goa, Tamil Nadu, Uttar Pradesh, Jammu & Kashmir, karnataka, Gujarat, Dadra and Nagar Haveli & Daman and Diu, Mizoram, Rajasthan, Ladakh, Andaman & Nicobar Islands, Chandigarh, Odisha, Lakshadweep, Sikkim and Puducherry. MyGov is part of Digital India Corporation, a Section 8 company under Ministry of Electronics and IT, Government of India. MyGov has had significant success in terms of engaging with citizens. Logos and Tagline of key National Projects have been crowdsourced through MyGov. Few Notable crowdsourced initiatives are Logo for Swachh Bharat, Logo for National Education Policy, Logo for Digital India Campaign, etc. MyGov has time and again solicited inputs of draft policies from citizens; a few of those are National Education Policy, Data Centre Policy, Data Protection Policy, National Ports Policy, IIM Bill etc. MyGov has also been frequently soliciting ideas for Mann Ki Baat, Annual Budget, Pariksha Pe Charcha and many more such initiatives. To disseminate authentic, easy to understand and consistent information relating to COVID-19, MyGov has been supporting MoHFW for communications on social media. With an objective to drive behavioural change, fighting fake news and busting myths, MyGov created a dedicated portal for COVID-19-related information dissemination – https://www.mygov.in/covid-19. MyGov has also built a Chatbot on WhatsApp to disseminate information about COVID-19 and Vaccination through a Helpdesk number 9013151515. In compliance with the Information Technology (Intermediary Guidelines and Digital Media Ethics Code) Rules, 2021, MyGov has notified the following officers as Chief Compliance Officer, Nodal Officer and Grievance Officer: | Officer | Name | Designation | | |---|---|---|---| | Chief Compliance Officer | Ajit Kumar | CEO MyGov | compliance[_]officer[at]mygov[dot]in | | Nodal Officer | Shobhendra Bahadur | Director, MyGov | nodalofficer[at]mygov[dot]in | | Grievance Officer | Grievance", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["about", "citizen", "frequently", "grievance", "guideline", "help", "info", "rules", "scheme", "wwwmygovin"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_wwwmygovin_cda7d7f3_01", "source_url": "https://www.mygov.in/simple-page/contact-us", "title": "Contact Us | MyGov", "section": "Overview", "text": "Working Hours: 09:00 hours to 17:30 hours (Saturday and Sunday Holidays) Office Address/Postal Address Office of CEO, MyGov 3rd Floor, Room no-3015 Ministry of Electronics and Information Technology (Government of India) Electronics Niketan, 6, CGO Complex, Lodhi Road, New Delhi - 110003 India e-Mail: connect[at]mygov[dot]nic[dot]in Log on to public grievance platform to lodge grievances for quick redressal Queries Related to Contests/ Quizzes or for Engagement with MyGov In compliance with the Information Technology (Intermediary Guidelines and Digital Media Ethics Code) Rules, 2021, MyGov has notified the following officers as Chief Compliance Officer, Nodal Officer and Grievance Officer: | Officer | Name | Designation | | |---|---|---|---| | Chief Compliance Officer | Ajit Kumar | CEO MyGov | compliance[_]officer[at]mygov[dot]in | | Nodal Officer | Shobhendra Bahadur | Director, MyGov | nodalofficer[at]mygov[dot]in | | Grievance Officer | Grievance Officer | Grievance Officer, MyGov | grievance[at]mygov[dot]in | For details you can visit the FAQ page. Any feedback, related to content, design, or technology with respect to the MyGov Portal may be submitted at Feedback section.", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["faq", "grievance", "guideline", "info", "lodge", "portal", "rules", "wwwmygovin"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_wwwmygovin_8fe67102_01", "source_url": "https://www.mygov.in/mygov-faq", "title": "MyGov - FAQ | MyGov", "section": "Overview", "text": "What is MyGov MyGov is an innovative platform to build a partnership between Citizens and Government with the help of technology for growth and development of India. Through this platform, the Government aims to encourage Citizen Participation towards Good Governance by seeking their ideas, suggestions and grass roots level contribution. Citizens can participate in this unique initiative of nation building. For the very first time in the history of this country, citizens from across India will come together to share their expert thoughts, ideas and suggestions with the Government in areas related to various policies, programs, schemes etc. MyGov aims to empower citizens to work hand in hand with the Government. How can I join MyGov Register on https://www.mygov.in to participate. You will be asked for personal details such as name, email id etc. You will also be required to mention the kind of skills you have & the issues on which you may like to provide inputs. Please note that MyGov do not share any personally identifiable information volunteered on this site with any third party (public/private). Any information provided to this website will be protected from loss, misuse, unauthorized access, disclosure, alteration, or destruction. For Government Employee If you are a Government Employee having @gov.in or @nic.in email Id, you can use the credentials for the same to log in without having to provide any other details. . For Public For the larger public, registration and sign up on MyGov can be done through your valid email ID and your 10-digit Mobile number. While logging in, either the registered mobile number or email id can be used. Every time you enter your Mobile Number or Email ID, a One Time Password (OTP) shall be sent to your email as well as mobile number registered with MyGov. You do not need to remember any password for logging in. Alternatively, you can Sign-in by using your email id and password as you maintain with MyGov. What are the modes of participation? The platform consists of various focus Groups where citizens can undertake tasks (both online and on ground) as well as share their insights through various tasks, discussions, polls, talks and blogs related to the particular Group. Groups: Collaborate with Government! Explore & choose from an array of topics on public and national importance on which Government and its respective agency would like to hear from you. Make yourself part of these groups and express your valued views and proposal on these issues. The Government would seek your active engagement and participation in addressing issues mentioned as group topics in the portal. A citizen can only be part of 4 groups at one particular time. Discuss: Express Yourself Express your valued insight and views on theme based discussions on the MyGov. It values your views and the Government is keen to hear from you to improve on its policy initiatives.", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["citizen", "help", "info", "portal", "registration", "scheme", "wwwmygovin"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_wwwmygovin_29eec3e8_01", "source_url": "https://www.mygov.in/simple-page/help", "title": "Help | MyGov", "section": "Overview", "text": "Are you finding it difficult to access/navigate through the content/pages of this Portal? This section attempts to help you have a pleasant experience while browsing this Portal. Sections of this Portal The Do and Discuss section provides information about all the tasks and discussions group wise. File Format: Viewing Information in Various File Formats The information provided by this website is available in Portable Document Format (PDF), and also in HTML format. To view the information properly, your browser needs to have the required plug-ins or software. For example, the pdf reader software is required to view the pdf format document. In case your system does not have this software, you can download it from the Internet for free. | Document Type | Plug-in for Download | |---|---| | | Adobe Acrobat Reader Convert a PDF file online into HTML or text format | | | Word Viewer | | | Excel Viewer | | | PowerPoint Viewer | | | Windows Media Player | Accessibility Help Use the accessibility options provided by this website to control the screen display. These options allow increasing the text size and changing the contrast scheme for clear visibility and better readability. Changing the Text Size Changing the size of the text refers to making the text appearing smaller or bigger from its standard size. There are three options provided to you to set the size of the text that affects the readability. These are: - Large: Displays information in the large font size. - Medium: Displays information in a standard font size, which is the default size. - Small: Displays information in the small font size.", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["about", "download", "help", "info", "portal", "scheme", "wwwmygovin"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_pgportalgovin_fbb01083_01", "source_url": "https://pgportal.gov.in/", "title": "CPGRAMS-Home", "section": "Overview", "text": "Any Grievance sent by email will not be attended to / entertained. Please lodge your grievance on this portal. ABOUT CPGRAMS Centralised Public Grievance Redress and Monitoring System (CPGRAMS) is an online platform available to the citizens 24x7 to lodge their grievances to the public authorities on any subject related to service delivery. It is a single portal connected to all the Ministries/Departments of Government of India and States. Every Ministry and States have role-based access to this system. CPGRAMS is also accessible to the citizens through standalone mobile application downloadable through Google Play store and mobile application integrated with UMANG. The status of the grievance filed in CPGRAMS can be tracked with the unique registration ID provided at the time of registration of the complainant. CPGRAMS also provides appeal facility to the citizens if they are not satisfied with the resolution by the Grievance Officer. After closure of grievance if the complainant is not satisfied with the resolution, he/she can provide feedback. If the rating is ‘Poor’ the option to file an appeal is enabled. The status of the Appeal can also be tracked by the petitioner with the grievance registration number. Issues which are not taken up for redress : - RTI Matters - Court related / Subjudice matters - Religious matters - Grievances of Government employees concerning their service matters including disciplinary proceedings etc. unless the aggrieved employee has already exhausted the prescribed channels keeping in view the DoPT OM No. 11013/08/2013-Estt.(A-III) dated 31.08.2015 - If you have not got a satifactory redress of your grievance within a reasonable period of time,relating to Ministries/Departments and Organisations under the purview of Directorate of Public Grievances(DPG), Cabinet Secretariat, GOI, you may seek help of DPG in resolution. Please click here for details. - Government is not charging fee from the public for filing grievances. All money being paid by the public for filing grievance is going only to M/s CSC only", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["about", "citizen", "grievance", "help", "pgportalgovin", "portal", "registration", "service", "status", "track"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_pgportalgovin_a63f9b3b_01", "source_url": "https://pgportal.gov.in/Home/Faq", "title": "Centralized Public Grievance Redress System - FAQs/Help", "section": "Overview", "text": "FAQ Frequently Asked Questions on Grievance Redress Mechanism in Government of India and the Role of Department of Administrative Reforms and Public Grievance, New Delhi, therein Department of Administrative Reforms and Public Grievances, 5th floor, Sardar Patel Bhavan, Sansad Marg, New Delhi – 110001 Website:: www.darpg.gov.in Tele fax : 23741006 The grievances can be sent to : - The Department of Administrative Reforms and Public Grievances. (pgportal.gov.in) - The Department of Pensions and Pensioners’ Welfare.(DP&PW) (pgportal.gov.in/pension/) The above nodal agencies receive grievances online through pgportal.gov.in as well as by post or by hand in person, from the public. The grievances can be lodged online on . In cases where internet facility is not available or even otherwise, the citizen is free to send her/his grievance by Post. There is no prescribed format. The grievance may be written on any plain sheet of paper or on a Postcard / Inland letter and addressed to the Department. The grievance can also be filled through Common Service Centre. The grievance is acknowledged online or by post. A unique registration number is given to each grievance. It may be tracked on the pgportal using view status link and after providing unique registration number. Every Central Ministry / Department has designated a Joint Secretary or a Director / Deputy Secretary, as its ‘Director of Grievances’. He / She is the nodal officer for redress of grievances on work areas allocated to that particular Ministry / Department. No. In such situations, the citizen will have to lodge a fresh grievance drawing reference to the closed grievance, and call for details. Sometimes, the details are sent by post and mentioned in the final report. The postal delivery may be awaited before lodging a fresh grievance The list is accessible on the Department’s website at In addition to this, it is also available in the Citizen’s Charter of the Ministries/Departments hosted on their websites. Every Wednesday of the week has been earmarked for receiving and hearing of grievances by the Director of Public Grievances in person. - Subjudice cases or any matter concerning judgment given by any court. - Personal and family disputes - RTI matters - Anything that impacts upon territorial integrity of the country or friendly relations with other countries The Department of Administrative Reforms & Public Grievances is the chief policy making, monitoring and coordinating Department for public grievances arising from the work of Ministries/Departments/Organizations of the Government of India. The grievances received in the department are forwarded to the Ministries/Departments concerned. Redressal of grievances is done by respective Ministries/Departments in a decentralized manner. The Department periodically reviews the status of redressal of public grievances under CPGRAMS of Ministries/Departments for speedy disposal of grievances / complaints. All grievances relating to State Governments / Union Territory Administrations and Government of NCT Region of Delhi, are sent to the State/ UT/ NCT Government concerned. Citizens may take", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["acts", "charter", "citizen", "faq", "frequently", "grievance", "pgportalgovin", "portal", "registration", "service"], "language": "en"}
