{"id": "civic_wwwmyschemegovin_c6c5d319_01", "source_url": "https://www.myscheme.gov.in/", "title": "myScheme", "section": "Overview", "text": "- #GOVERNMENTSCHEMES - #SCHEMESFORYOU CategoriesStates/UTsCentral Ministries Find schemes based on categories How it works Easy steps to apply for Government Schemes Enter Details Start by entering your basic details! Search Our search engine will find the relevant schemes! Select & Apply Select and apply for the best suited scheme About myScheme is a National Platform that aims to offer one-stop search and discovery of the Government schemes. It provides an innovative, technology-based solution to discover scheme information based upon the eligibility of the citizen. The platform helps the citizen to find the right Government schemes for them. It also guides on how to apply for different Government schemes. Thus no need to visit multiple Government websites. Frequently Asked Questions Checkout our knowledge base for some of your answers! What is myScheme, and how is it different from other government portals? How will myScheme help common citizens? How does myScheme work? What is the procedure for knowing the right scheme on the myScheme platform? What information about a particular scheme can I find on myScheme?", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["about", "apply", "citizen", "eligibility", "frequently", "help", "info", "procedure", "scheme", "wwwmyschemegovin"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_wwwmyschemegovin_7101617f_01", "source_url": "https://www.myscheme.gov.in/about", "title": "MyScheme Aggregator - View More", "section": "Overview", "text": "About Us - Home - About Us - Our Vision Our vision is to make citizens life easier Our Mission - Our mission is to streamline the government - user interface for government schemes and benefits. - Reduce time and effort required to find and avail a government scheme myScheme is a National Platform that aims to offer one-stop search and discovery of the Government schemes. It provides an innovative, technology-based solution to discover scheme information based upon the eligibility of the citizen. The platform helps the citizen to find the right Government schemes for them. It also guides on how to apply for different Government schemes. Thus no need to visit multiple Government websites. myScheme platform is Developed, Managed, and Operated by National e-Governance Division (NeGD), with the Support of Ministry of Electronics and Information Technology (MeitY), Department of Administrative Reforms and Public Grievance (DARPG) and in partnership with other Central and State Ministries/Departments. Eligibility Check You can check your eligibility for schemes using different criteria and personal attribute Scheme Finder Fast and easy searching with filter based drill downs for various Government Schemes Scheme in detail Deep dive into dedicated scheme pages for fine grained scheme details before you apply", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["about", "apply", "citizen", "eligibility", "grievance", "help", "info", "scheme", "wwwmyschemegovin"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_wwwmyschemegovin_cc37a3fd_01", "source_url": "https://www.myscheme.gov.in/faqs", "title": "MyScheme Aggregator - View More", "section": "Overview", "text": "What is myScheme, and how is it different from other government portals? myScheme is a national platform for accessing a wide range of government schemes from both the Central & State/UT Governments. It is a one-stop platform for search & discovery of government schemes based on demographic details. Unlike traditional government portals, myScheme brings together schemes from the Central Government, State Governments, and Union Territories on a single platform and helps users find relevant schemes based on their eligibility. How will myScheme help common citizens? The myScheme platform simplifies access to government schemes by enabling citizens to discover relevant schemes in one place, eliminating the need to visit multiple departmental websites or review extensive scheme guidelines to check their eligibility. How does myScheme work? The myScheme platform follows a simple and user-friendly three-step process to help citizens discover government schemes for which they are eligible: Step 1: The user enters basic details such as demographic, income, social category, etc. Step 2: Based on the information provided, myScheme displays relevant schemes from hundreds of government schemes for the user. Step 3: The user can select from the list of eligible schemes and get more information from the dedicated scheme page with detailed knowledge, FAQs, and application process and navigate to the respective application URL to apply. What is the procedure for knowing the right scheme on the myScheme platform? To find the right scheme on the myScheme platform, citizens can begin by visiting the platform's official website. Once on the homepage, they will find the 'Find Schemes for You' feature, which allows users to enter their demographic details, such as age, gender, income level, category, etc. Once these details are submitted, the platform will provide a list of relevant schemes based on the user's profile. What information about a particular scheme can I find on myScheme? The myScheme platform provides comprehensive information on each scheme, including eligibility criteria, benefits offered, application procedure, and the documents required to avail the scheme. It also features a dedicated Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) section to address common queries related to the scheme. What are the broad categories under which schemes are available on myScheme? The schemes available on the myScheme platform are broadly classified into 15 categories based on their nature of benefits and target beneficiaries. These categories include Agriculture, Rural & Environment; Banking, Financial Services & Insurance; Business & Entrepreneurship; Education & Learning; Health & Wellness; Housing & Shelter; Public Safety, Law & Justice; Science, IT & Communications; Skills & Employment; Social Welfare & Empowerment; Sports & Culture; Transport & Infrastructure; Travel & Tourism; Utility & Sanitation; and Women & Child. Does the myScheme platform provide multilingual support? Yes, the myScheme platform currently supports content in 15 languages, including English. Support for additional Indian languages will be provided soon. Does the myScheme platform showcase both Central and State/UT-specific schemes? Yes, the myScheme platform currently", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["about", "citizen", "faq", "frequently", "guideline", "procedure", "process", "scheme", "service", "wwwmyschemegovin"], "language": "en"}
