d may kindly be brought to our notice. please e-mail at : supremecourt[at]nic[dot]in", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["documents", "info", "scigovin", "service"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_scigovin_7a119abb_01", "source_url": "https://www.sci.gov.in/about-department/history/", "title": "History | Supreme Court of India | India", "section": "Overview", "text": "History The Supreme Court of India is the apex judicial body under the Constitution of India. Article 124 of the Constitution states that “There shall be a Supreme Court of India.” The Supreme Court came into existence on 26 January 1950 with the coming into force of the Constitution. The Supreme Court initially functioned from the old Parliament House till it moved to the present building located on Tilak Marg, New Delhi in 1958. On 28 January 1950, two days after India became a Sovereign Democratic Republic, the Supreme Court was inaugurated. The inauguration took place in the Chamber of Princes in the old Parliament building where the Federal Court of India sat for 12 years from 1937 to 1950. The inaugural proceedings began at 9:45 am. It was attended by the first Chief Justice of India, Harilal J. Kania and Judges of the Federal Court – Justices Saiyid Fazl Ali, M. Patanjali Sastri, Mehr Chand Mahajan, Bijan Kumar Mukherjea and S.R. Das, the Chief Justices of the High Courts of Allahabad, Bombay, Madras, Orissa, Assam, Nagpur, Punjab, Saurashtra, Patiala and the East Punjab States Union, Mysore, Hyderabad, Madhya Bharat and Travancore-Cochin. The proceedings were also graced by the Prime Minister of India, ambassadors and diplomatic representatives of foreign States, the Attorney General of India M.C. Setalvad, the Advocate Generals of Bombay, Madras, Uttar Pradesh, Bihar, East Punjab, Orissa, Mysore, Hyderabad, and Madhya Bharat and a large number of advocates. To ensure that the Rules of the Supreme Court were published and the names of all the Advocates and agents of the Federal Court were brought on the rolls of the Supreme Court, the inaugural proceedings were put as part of the record of the Supreme Court. After its inauguration on 28 January 1950, the Supreme Court commenced its sittings in a part of the old Parliament House. The Court moved into a new building in 1958. The first President of India Dr. Rajendra Prasad inaugurated the present building of the Supreme Court of India on 4 August 1958. The building is shaped to project the image of scales of justice. It has a 27.6 metre high dome and a spacious colonnaded verandah. The Central Wing of the building is the centre beam of the scales. The Chief Justice’s Court is the largest of the courts located in the centre of the Central Wing. There is a life size figure of Mahatma Gandhi, the apostle of truth and non-violence in the courtyard opposite the Chief Justice’s Court. The statue was unveiled by the 26th Chief Justice of India, Justice A.M. Ahmadi on 1 August 1996. There is also a 7-foot tall statue of Dr. B.R. Ambedkar which was unveiled by Hon’ble President of India, Smt. Droupadi Murmu in the presence of the 50th Chief Justice of India, Dr. Justice D.Y. Chandrachud on 26 November 2023. The statue honours the architect", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["rules", "scigovin"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_ecommitteescigovin_42e278c6_01", "source_url": "https://ecommitteesci.gov.in/", "title": "Homepage | Official Website of e-Committee, Supreme Court of India | India", "section": "Overview", "text": "About e-Committee The e-Committee, Supreme Court of India, welcomes you to this portal showcasing the Information and Communication Technology (ICT) initiatives adopted by the judicial system in India. …. Latest Announcements Latest News OFFICERS OF eCommittee, Supreme Court of India Shri Pushpender Singh Member(J) (Processes) Dr. Saleena V G Nair Registrar (J) Mr. Shubham Vashist Member (J) (Project Management) Mr. Ashish J. Shiradhonkar Member (Systems) Digital initiatives VIRTUAL COURTS Virtual Courts is a concept, aimed at eliminating the presence… ePay ECOURTS FEE PAYMENT ECOURTS SERVICES MOBILE APP eCourts services mobile application received the Digital India award as a revolutionary court information tool in the country. TOUCH SCREEN KIOSKS Touch screen kiosks are installed at various court complexes across the country. NATIONAL JUDICIAL DATA GRID NJDG, a flagship project implemented under the aegis of the eCourts project, has been recognized as a significant innovation under the Ease of Doing Business initiative of the Government of India.", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["about", "ecommitteescigovin", "info", "portal", "process", "service"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_ecommitteescigovin_77db99aa_01", "source_url": "https://ecommitteesci.gov.in/services/", "title": "Citizen Centric Services | Official Website of e-Committee, Supreme Court of India | India", "section": "Overview", "text": "Virtual Courts is a concept, aimed at eliminating the presence… Service enabling online payment of court fee, fine, penalty and… eCourts services mobile application received the Digital India award as… A central repository of information and data pertaining to High… A centralised gateway providing links to several initiatives and services… A centralised gateway providing links to all the e-Courts services… Touch screen kiosks are installed at various court complexes across… The CIS software is designed to automatically send emails to… For litigants who do not have internet connectivity case details… A centralised portal leading a user to the individual District… e-Sewa Kendras have been created in the High Courts and… e-Filing system enables electronic filing of legal papers. Using e-filing,… Case status is being sent automatically to registered Advocates and… NJDG, a flagship project implemented under the aegis of the… Digital Courts – Green Initiative of Indian Judiciary has been…", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["ecommitteescigovin", "info", "portal", "service", "status"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_ecommitteescigovin_0ddd48e7_01", "source_url": "https://ecommitteesci.gov.in/service/ecourts-services-portal/", "title": "ECOURTS SERVICES PORTAL | Official Website of e-Committee, Supreme Court of India | India", "section": "Overview", "text": "ECOURTS SERVICES PORTAL A centralised gateway providing links to several initiatives and services provided under the eCourts project. It enables stakeholders such as citizens, litigants, lawyers, government and law enforcement agencies to access data and information relating to the judicial system of the country. The eCourts National portal works as an online repository of data providing a host of services and diverse information such as: - Cause list - Case Status: Case Status may be accessed across various search parameters such as case number, FIR Number, party name, advocate name, filing number, Act or case type - Daily orders and final judgments: Orders and final judgments can be similarly accessed through CNR number, Case Number, Court Number, Party Name and Order Date. Visit : http://services.ecourts.gov.in", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["citizen", "ecommitteescigovin", "info", "portal", "service", "status"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_ecommitteescigovin_b38b4ec5_01", "source_url": "https://ecommitteesci.gov.in/the-ecommittee-supreme-court-of-india-in-collaboration-with-nalsa-and-the-department-of-justice-government-of-india-will-organise-the-flag-off-ceremony-of-mobile-esewa-vans-on-se/", "title": "e-Committee, Supreme Court of India - eCommittee, SCI in collaboration with NALSA & DOJ, GoI organised ‘Flag-Off Ceremony’ of Mobile eSewa Vans, taking eCourts Services & Legal Aid directly to citizens’ doorsteps", "section": "Overview", "text": "The eCommittee, Supreme Court of India, in collaboration with NALSA and the Department of Justice, Government of India, will organise the “Flag-Off Ceremony” of Mobile eSewa Vans on September 4, 2026. eCommittee, SCI in collaboration with NALSA & DOJ, GoI organised ‘Flag-Off Ceremony’ of Mobile eSewa Vans, taking eCourts Services & Legal Aid directly to citizens’ doorsteps Publish Date: September 4, 2026 Press Release dated September 4, 2026 eCommittee, Supreme Court of India 04.09.2026 PRESS RELEASE eCommittee, Supreme Court of India, in collaboration with the National Legal Services Authority (NALSA) and the Department of Justice, Government of India, organised the “Flag-Off Ceremony” of Mobile eSewa Vans, taking eCourts services and legal aid directly to citizens’ doorsteps A “Flag-Off Ceremony” of Mobile eSewa Vans, an initiative of the eCourts Project, was held today, Friday, the 4th of September, 2026, at the AB Lobby, Administrative Buildings Complex, Supreme Court of India, New Delhi, under the joint aegis of the eCommittee, Supreme Court of India, and the National Legal Services Authority (NALSA), in collaboration with the Department of Justice, Government of India. The Mobile eSewa Vans were flagged off by Hon’ble Mr. Justice Surya Kant, Chief Justice of India and Patron-in-Chief, eCommittee, Supreme Court of India, in the august presence of Hon’ble Mr. Justice Vikram Nath, Judge, Supreme Court of India and Chairman, eCommittee, Hon’ble Mrs. Justice B.V. Nagarathna, Judge, Supreme Court of India, Hon’ble Mr. Justice Pamidighantam Sri Narasimha, Judge, Supreme Court of India, Hon’ble Mr. Justice Arun Palli, Judge, Supreme Court of India, Shri Arjun Ram Meghwal, Minister of State (Independent Charge), Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India, R. Venkataramani, Attorney General of India and Justice Anjani Kumar Mishra, Vice Chairman, eCommittee, Supreme Court of India. Prior to the flag-off of the Mobile eSewa Vans, Hon’ble Mr. Justice Surya Kant, Chief Justice of India and Patron-in-Chief, eCommittee, Supreme Court of India, personally inspected and witnessed the comprehensive technological features and infrastructure of the Mobile eSewa Vans. Demonstrating the van’s high-definition video conferencing capabilities and high-speed multi-network connectivity, the Hon’ble Chief Justice of India connected live with the High Court and the District Court, directly from Mobile eSewa Van. The live interaction validated the efficacy of the onboard digital systems, establishing the Van’s readiness to conduct seamless remote court proceedings, virtual hearings, and citizen-centric judicial engagements directly from the field. Twenty-six Mobile eSewa Vans were launched from the Supreme Court of India at today’s ceremony, the first tranche of a larger fleet of 73 Mobile eSewa Vans that will be progressively deployed across designated High Court and District Court jurisdictions across the country. About the Initiative The Mobile eSewa Van is designed to bring eCourts services, legal aid, and dispute resolution directly to every citizen, bridging the digital divide and ensuring universal access to justice. Conceived as an extension of the eCourts Project, the initiative seeks to carry the reach", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["about", "citizen", "ecommitteescigovin", "service"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_ecommitteescigovin_687e5926_01", "source_url": "https://ecommitteesci.gov.in/about-e-committee/", "title": "e-Committee, Supreme Court of India - About e-Committee", "section": "Overview", "text": "Accessibility Tools Accessibility Tools Color Contrast High Contrast Normal Contrast Highlight Links Invert Saturation Text Size Font Size Increase Font Size Decrease Normal Font Text Spacing Line Height Others Hide Images Big Cursor इ-कमिटी, उच्चतम न्यायालय, भारत e-Committee, Supreme Court of India इ-कमिटी, उच्चतम न्यायालय, भारत e-Committee, Supreme Court of India Information and Communication Technology in Indian Judiciary Search Search Menu Toggle More Home About e-Committee Introduction Vision & Objectives Administrative Setup e-Courts NIC Team Former Members of eCommittee Awards & Appreciations Significant Achievements Future initiatives/Work in progress Virtual Courts Video Conference NSTEP Citizen’s Corner Citizen Centric Services Integration with other Government Department e-Payments LIMBS ICJS e-Prisons Manuals Documents Policy and Action Plan Documents Sanction Orders Model Rules Objective Accomplishment Report Training and Awareness Programmes Standard Operating Procedure (SOP) Media Publications Newsletters Brochures ICT Initiatives News Gallery Photo Gallery Video Gallery Audio Gallery High Courts Best Practice of High Court District Judiciary Case Management through CIS 4.0 Case Management through CIS 3.0 Court Management tool JustIS App Help desk for official email – @aij.gov.in Mobile app SANDES Judges Login Judges Category Close Home About e-committee Share on Facebook Share of X (formerly Twitter) Share on Linkedin About e-committee Introduction Vision and Objectives Administrative Setup Ecourts NIC Team Awards and Appreciations Significant Achievements", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["about", "citizen", "documents", "ecommitteescigovin", "help", "info", "manual", "procedure", "rules", "service"], "language": "hi"}
{"id": "civic_filingecourtsgovin_93488bee_01", "source_url": "https://filing.ecourts.gov.in/pdedev/", "title": "eFiling Services | eFiling Login Form", "section": "Overview", "text": "Your cases may take some time to refresh after being imported. Do you want to delete my cases ? DeleteCancel Future Prospects While determining the income, an addition of 50% of actual salary to the income of the deceased towards future prospects, where the deceased had a permanent job and was below the age of 40 years, should be made. The addition should be 30%, if the age of the deceased was 48 between 40 to 50 years. In case the deceased was between the age of 50 to 60 years, the addition should be 15%. Actual salary should be read as actual salary less tax. (iv) In case the deceased was self-employed or on a fixed salary, an addition of 40% of the established income should be the warrant where the deceased was below the age of 40 years. An addition of 25% where the deceased was between the age of 40 to 50 years and 10% where the deceased was between the age of 50 to 60 years should be regarded as the necessary method of computation. The established income means the income minus the tax component. Sr. No. Requirements Future Prospects 1 Employment type : Permanent (Age <40) Add 50% of Actual Salary 2 Employment type : Permanent (Age >=40 and <50) Add 30% of Actual Salary 3 Employment type : Permanent (Age >=50 and <60) Add 15% of Actual Salary 4 Employment type : Permanent (Age >=60) 0 5 Employment type : Temporary/Fixed Income/Business (Age <40) Add 40% of Actual Income 6 Employment type : Temporary/Fixed Income/Business (Age >=40 and <50) Add 25% of Actual Salary 7 Employment type : Temporary/Fixed Income/Business (Age >=50 and <60) Add 10% of Actual Salary 8 Employment type : Temporary/Fixed Income/Business (Age >=60) 0 Deduction towards personal and living expenses Where the deceased was married, the deduction towards personal and living expenses of the deceased should be one-third (1/3rd) where the number of dependent family members is 2 to 3, one-fourth (1/4th) where the number of dependent family members is 4 to 6, and one-fifth (1/5th) where the number of dependent family members exceeds six. Where the deceased was a bachelor and the claimants are the parents, normally 50% is deducted as personal and living expenses ... e-Filing system is a complete end to end solution developed for online filing of plaints, written statements, replies and various applications related to cases. Both Civil and Criminal cases can be filed before any High Court or District Court of the country. It is designed in Bilingual (English and local language) to reach wider group covering advocates/litigants. e-Filing system provides several benefits Save time, money, travel of advocates and clients Obviate the need to physically visit the court Reduce the need of meetings between clients and advocates Automatic digitization of case records Positive impact on environment by reducing paper footprint e-Filing system enables", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["filingecourtsgovin"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_uidaigovin_cba4f87a_01", "source_url": "https://uidai.gov.in/en", "title": "Home - Unique Identification Authority of India | Government of India - Unique Identification Authority of India | Government of India", "section": "Overview", "text": "Enrolment | Get BaalAadhaar | Mandatory Biometric Update Visit your nearest Aadhaar Seva Kendra for service that needs to be done in person The Unique Identification Authority of India (UIDAI) is a statutory authority established under the provisions of the Aadhaar (Targeted Delivery of Financial and Other Subsidies, Benefits and Services) Act, 2016 (“Aadhaar Act 2016”) on 12 July 2016 by the Government of India, under the Ministry of Electronics and Information Technology (MeitY). The Aadhaar Act 2016 has been amended by the Aadhaar and Other Laws (Amendment) Act, 2019 (14 of 2019) w.e.f. 25.07.2019. Announcements NEW Official Memorandums Press Release Circulars Tenders Three-month Preventive Vigilance Campaign from 17th August 2026 to 16th November 2026 and Observance of Vigilance Awareness Week 2026 from 26th October 2026 to 01st November 2026 on Theme: “सत्यनिष्ठा से समॄद्धि” / “Probity for Prosperity” Oct 21, 2026 CEO Message on Hindi Diwas Sep 9, 2026 Play Book on Ease of Onboarding 145.32 Aadhaar Enrolments 2,632.51 EKYC Transactions 2.45 Registered Devices How to register on Aadhaar App and login OVSE use cases video Aadhaar App Launch Video How to download the Aadhaar app? How to register on the Aadhaar app? Which services are available on this app? What details are required for onboarding on the Aadhaar app?", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["download", "info", "service", "uidaigovin"], "language": "hi"}
{"id": "civic_uidaigovin_9c8361b2_01", "source_url": "https://uidai.gov.in/hi/about-uidai", "title": "Unique Identification Authority of India (UIDAI) - About UIDAI", "section": "Overview", "text": "About UIDAI In this section Who we are People at UIDAI Our Offices Careers Transparency and Accountability Legal Framework Aadhaar Dashboard UIDAI traces its origins to the 2006 UID initiatives, evolving into a statutory authority tasked with building a robust digital identity system and streamlining service delivery for residents across India. At the Unique Identification Authority of India, leadership comprises Chairperson Neelkanth Mishra, members Prof. Mausam and Nilesh Shah, and CEO Bhuvnesh Kumar. Supported by experienced officers and strong policies, UIDAI ensures effective governance, secure Aadhaar services, and a transparent, inclusive work environment. The Unique Identification Authority of India operates from its New Delhi HO, 8 Regional Offices and State Offices across India, with data centres in Bengaluru and Manesar, ensuring nationwide reach and efficient service delivery. In this section, we explore career opportunities at the Unique Identification Authority of India through deputation, internships, internal consultancy, volunteer roles, and sabbaticals, offering diverse ways to contribute and grow. The Right to Information Act, 2005 enables citizens to access information held by public authorities, promoting transparency and accountability. It allows inspection of records, obtaining certified copies, and access to electronic data, ensuring openness in governance and empowering citizens to stay informed about public administration. Access UIDAI’s legal framework, including the Aadhaar Act 2016, amendments, ordinances, and related laws governing identity, authentication, and service delivery in India. View key Aadhaar statistics, including enrolments, updates, authentications, eKYC transactions, and registered devices, reflecting the scale and reach of UIDAI services across India. Content Information Published on:11 Apr 2026 Last Updated:07 Oct 2026 View more F.A.Qs Content Information Published on:11 Apr 2026 Last Updated:07 Oct 2026", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["about", "citizen", "info", "service", "uidaigovin"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_pmkisangovin_96660348_01", "source_url": "https://pmkisan.gov.in/", "title": "PM-Kisan Samman Nidhi", "section": "Overview", "text": "Department of Agriculture and Farmers Welfare Ministry of Agriculture and Farmers Welfare Government of India eKYC is MANDATORY for PMKISAN Registered Farmers. Biometric-based eKYC option is now available for CSC VLE Logins, PM-KISAN Mobile Application and State Authorized User Logins. - The Department has identified certain suspected cases that may fall under the exclusion criteria outlined in the PM-KISAN scheme guidelines. These include, for example: - (i) Farmers who acquired land ownership after 01-02-2019, - (ii) Cases where more than one family member is receiving benefits (e.g., both husband and wife, an adult member and minor, etc.). - The benefits for such cases have been temporarily withheld till physical verification is completed. - Farmers are requested to check their eligibility status on Know Your Status (KYS) of PM KISAN website/ mobile app or Kisan eMitra chatbot for further details. Period Wise Number of Farmers Benefited - 9,44,65,646 APR-JUL 2026-27 - 9,46,15,309 DEC-MAR 2025-26 - 9,35,79,869 AUG-NOV 2025-26 - 9,71,41,402 APR-JUL 2025-26 - 10,06,85,615 DEC-MAR 2024-25 - 9,59,28,628 AUG-NOV 2024-25 - 9,38,01,580 APR-JUL 2024-25 - 9,04,44,694 DEC-MAR 2023-24 - 8,12,16,697 AUG-NOV 2023-24 - 8,56,79,091 APR-JUL 2023-24 - 8,12,38,919 DEC-MAR 2022-23 - 8,57,40,741 AUG-NOV 2022-23 - 10,48,45,164 APR-JUL 2022-23 - 10,41,68,513 DEC-MAR 2021-22 - 10,34,47,290 AUG-NOV 2021-22 - 9,99,17,958 APR-JUL 2021-22 - 9,84,76,200 DEC-MAR 2020-21 - 9,72,27,546 AUG-NOV 2020-21 - 9,26,93,999 APR-JUL 2020-21 - 8,20,91,667 DEC-MAR 2019-20 - 7,66,01,029 AUG-NOV 2019-20 - 6,00,34,872 APR-JUL 2019-20 - 3,16,21,743 DEC-MAR 2018-19 Payment Success Scheme Exclusion The following categories of beneificiaries of higher economic status shall not be elligible for benefit under the scheme. - All Institutional Land holders. - Farmer families which belong to one or more of the following categories:. - Former and present holders of constitutional posts - Former and present Ministers/ State Ministers and former/present Members of LokSabha/ RajyaSabha/ State Legislative Assemblies/ State Legislative Councils,former and present Mayors of Municipal Corporations, former and present Chairpersons of District Panchayats. - All serving or retired officers and employees of Central/ State Government Ministries /Offices/Departments and its field units Central or State PSEs and Attached offices /Autonomous Institutions under Government as well as regular employees of the Local Bodies (Excluding Multi Tasking Staff /Class IV/Group D employees) - All superannuated/retired pensioners whose monthly pension is Rs.10,000/-or more (Excluding Multi Tasking Staff / Class IV/Group D employees) of above category - All Persons who paid Income Tax in last assessment year - Professionals like Doctors, Engineers, Lawyers, Chartered Accountants, and Architects registered with Professional bodies and carrying out profession by undertaking practices.", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["charter", "eligibility", "guideline", "pmkisangovin", "scheme", "status"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_pmkisangovin_1aab2e15_01", "source_url": "https://pmkisan.gov.in/Contacts.aspx", "title": "PM Kisan Samman Nidhi - Contact Us", "section": "Overview", "text": "Shri Atish Chandra, Secretary, Department of Agriculture and Farmers Welfare, Krishi Bhawan, New Delhi-110001. Shri Pramod Kumar Meherda, Additional Secretary (Farmers Welfare/Digital Agriculture/CEO (PM-KISAN)/IC/G-20/PP, Department of Agriculture and Farmers Welfare, Krishi Bhawan, New Delhi-110001. Shri Abhijit Phukon, Joint Secretary (Farmers Welfare), Department of Agriculture and Farmers Welfare, Krishi Bhawan, New Delhi-110001.", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["pmkisangovin"], "language": "en"}
