{"id": "civic_indianvisaonlinegovin_58dfc6ee_01", "source_url": "https://indianvisaonline.gov.in/", "title": "India Visa Online", "section": "Overview", "text": "All foreign nationals entering India are required to possess a valid international travel document in the form of a national passport with a valid visa from an Indian Mission/Post or eVisa (Limited Categories) from Bureau of Immigration, Ministry of Home Affairs. Visa on Arrival for the nationals of Japan, South Korea and UAE (only for such UAE nationals who had earlier obtained e-Visa or regular/paper visa for India) Available at selected Airports Advisory: The Government of India does not authorize any agent or intermediaries to charge fees for emergency, express visa, eVisas and eArrival card. A valid passport and a regular visa or eVisa or OCI card / eOCI (issued to various categories of Persons of Indian Origin) are required for entry into India, except for those exempted under bilateral arrangements. Foreign Nationals and OCI/eOCI cardholders must complete and submit the eArrival Card (https://indianvisaonline.gov.in/earrival/). All Passengers must also fill the Self-Declaration Form (https://airsuvidha.civilaviation.gov.in/) before reaching the Arrival Immigration Counters", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["indianvisaonlinegovin"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_indianvisaonlinegovin_85f2ea5d_01", "source_url": "https://indianvisaonline.gov.in/visa/index.html", "title": "Indian Visa Online (e-Visa) - For Regular/Paper visa by Indian Mission/Post, Apply here.", "section": "Overview", "text": "Fill and Submit Visa Application Form Securely. Submit your application with required documents at Indian Visa Application Center or at Indian Mission. Collect your passport/visa from Indian Mission/Visa Application Center or by post. Applicants may fill the online application form by going to the tab placed below. Once the form is filled and submitted, applicant must print the completed application form and sign and submit the physical copy along with the supporting documents and the Passport to the concerned Indian Visa Application Center (IVAC) or directly at the Indian Mission on the scheduled appointed date. The instructions for filling the form and scheduling the appointment can be seen at Instructions for Regular Visa Application. The status of Visa Application can be seen on the link for Visa Enquiry. The applicants are also requested to visit website of the Indian Mission concerned for detailed information about Indian visa.", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["about", "documents", "indianvisaonlinegovin", "info", "status"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_indianvisaonlinegovin_eb1061c0_01", "source_url": "https://indianvisaonline.gov.in/evisa/tvoa.html", "title": "Indian Visa Online (e-Visa) - For eVisa by Bureau of Immigration, Apply here.", "section": "Overview", "text": "Select option no. 6 on IVR to connect to agents. From rest of the countries none toll free number to India + 91-40-6717-4100 (Paid Number). Upload Photo and Passport Page Using Credit / Debit card / Payment Wallet Electronic Travel Authorization/ETA Will be sent to your e-mail Print ETA and present at Immigration Check Post where eVisa will be stamped on passport. Government of India makes no provision of charging of any emergency fees or additional fees for grant of any emergency / express e-visa. Those travelling to India are also advised to go through instructions available on the website of Bureau of Immigration at https://boi.gov.in. One Month (30 Days). Entries: Multiple Entry, non-extendable and non-convertible One year (365 Days) from the date of grant of ETA. Entries: Multiple Five years from the date of grant of ETA. Entries: Maximum stay in India during one Calender Year should not exceed 180 days for 1 year and 5 year Tourist Visa. 6 month from the date of grant of ETA. One year (365 days) from the date of grant of ETA. Continuous stay during each visit shall not exceed 180 days. If the intension is to stay for more then 180 days, shall get registered with FRRO/FRO concerned within two weeks after the expiry of 180 days. Thirty days (30 days) from the date of arrival into India. Organizers to upload all details & documentation on the MHA website (conference.mha.gov.in) One year (365 days) from the date of arrival into India. If the applicant is unable to complete his e-visa application form, he may save the application and may return to complete the application form by clicking the tab at the bottom of page: After your eVisa applications is submitted, the same shall be scrutinized and if any Document/Image is not appropriate, you may be advised on your given e-mail to re-upload the same. To re-upload use the tab at the bottom of the page. Applicant should normally receive this mail within 24 hours. The documents required for completing the eVisa application is indicated against each type of eVisa. Please keep all these documents ready at hand before beginning to fill your eVisa application. All documents including Business cards, Invitation letters etc. must be in English language, failing which the application would be liable for rejection. The entire process may take 10 to 15 minutes to complete the application and make the payment. Applicants must be fill eVisa application himself/herself and give correct information in each column and take responsibility for the correctness of information provided. SBIePay is the Payment Aggregator service of State Bank of India, India's Largest Bank and amongst top 50 Banks in the world, which provides bouquet of multiple payment options on a single page for the convenience of the customers. SBIePay has facilitated the following channels on e-Visa platform: SBIePay is certified with Payment Card Industry", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["documents", "indianvisaonlinegovin", "info", "process", "service"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_indianvisaonlinegovin_fab325fe_01", "source_url": "https://indianvisaonline.gov.in/avisa/index.html", "title": "Indian Visa Online (e-Visa) - AFGHAN Visa (For Afghanistan Nationals) Apply here.", "section": "Overview", "text": "1) Those coming to establish an industrial/business venture, those required to travel frequently on long-term business activities and for investors. 2) All other business activities (other than those covered above). 3) Sports persons and coaches including those engaged in commercial sports events in India on contract with remuneration. 4) As dependent of those coming to establish an industrial/business venture, those required to travel frequently on long-term business activities and for investors. 5) As dependent of business person coming for all other business activities (other than those covered above) and sports persons. Entry Multiple Duration 1 Year Documents required Copy of Passport page containing personal particulars National ID Card (Tazkira) One Letter of invitation from an Indian Company. One original signed letter from the company in the country of residence. Letter of recommendation from Afghan chamber of commerce OR Letter of recommendation from Indian Chambers of Commerce Any Proof of Residence in Afghanistan (optional) Any Proof of Occupation (optional) Entry Multiple Duration 1 Year Documents required Copy of Passport page containing personal particulars National ID Card (Tazkira) One Letter of invitation from an Indian Company. One original signed letter from the company in the country of residence. Letter of recommendation from Afghan chamber of commerce OR Letter of recommendation from Indian Chambers of Commerce Any Proof of Residence in Afghanistan (optional) Any Proof of Occupation (optional) Entry Multiple Duration 6 Months or for the duration of assignment whichever is earlier. Documents required Copy of Passport page containing personal particulars National ID Card (Tazkira) Approval of the Government of India in the Ministry of Youth Affairs and Sports (Department of Sports) Letter from the Organizing committee In India Document in support of Tax compliance on previous visit, if applicable Any Proof of Residence in Afghanistan (optional) Any Proof of Occupation (optional) Entry Multiple Duration (Visa validity should be co-terminus with the visa validity of the main applicant) Documents required Copy of Passport page containing personal particulars National ID Card (Tazkira) Relationship certificate (Birth/Marriage) Any Proof of Residence in Afghanistan (optional) Any Proof of Occupation (optional) Entry Multiple Duration (Visa validity should be co-terminus with the visa validity of the main applicant) Documents required Copy of Passport page containing personal particulars National ID Card (Tazkira) Relationship certificate (Birth/Marriage) Any Proof of Residence in Afghanistan (optional) Any Proof of Occupation (optional) Student Visa Purpose of Visit ICCR scholarship awardees. For admission in full time(structured) courses at educational institutions(Central/State Government Education Institutions & Private Education Institutions) Students who had previously held a valid Student Visa and who wish to return to India to continue/complete their studies. Spouse/Children of an Afghan national coming on Student Visa for higher studies (graduation and above) and research. Entry Four Duration Visa validity should be commensurate with the duration of educational course in India. Documents required Copy of Passport page containing personal particulars National ID Card (Tazkira) Documentation regarding award", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["documents", "frequently", "indianvisaonlinegovin"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_indiancitizenshiponlineni_735a2388_01", "source_url": "https://indiancitizenshiponline.nic.in/", "title": "Indian Citizenship Online", "section": "Overview", "text": "About Indian Citizenship Indian citizenship can be acquired by birth, descent, registration and naturalization. The conditions and procedure for acquisition of Indian citizenship as per the provision of the Citizenship Act, 1955 can be read at the Link : Acquisition Orders and Circulars Online Services - Citizenship Amendment Act (CAA) Acquisition of Indian citizenship A special provision exists for the submission of applications for Indian Citizenship under the Citizenship Amendment Act of 2019. It is specifically for individuals who entered India on or before 31st December, 2014, and belonging to Hindu or Sikh or Buddhist or Jain or Parsi or Christian community from Pakistan or Afghanistan or Bangladesh. For more detailed information, individuals may refer to the provisions outlined in the Citizenship Act of 1955. Individuals who wish to submit an application must have their own unique email ID and mobile number. Applicant may click on button \"click to submit application for Indian Citizenship under CAA 2019\" and log in using your personal email ID and mobile number. Citizenship Amendment Act (CAA) - FAQ's CITIZENSHIP AMENDMENT ACT (CAA) Frequently Asked Questions - (i) Who entered into India on or before 31.12.2014; and - (ii) Who has been exempted by or under section 3(2)(c) of the Passport (Entry into India) Act, 1920 or from the application of the provisions of the Foreigners Act, 1946 or any rule or order made thereunder. | S.No. | Form Number | Category of persons eligible | |---|---|---| | 1 | IIA | A person of Indian origin, for registration as a citizen of India | | 2 | IIIA | A person who is married to a citizen of India for registration as a citizen of India | | 3 | IVA | A person who is a minor child of a person who is a citizen of India, for registration as a citizen of India | | 4 | VA | A person whose parents are registered as a citizen of India, for registration as a citizen of India | | 5 | VIA | A person who or either of the parents was a citizen of Independent India, for registration as a citizen of India | | 6 | VIIA | A person who is registered as an Overseas Citizen of India Cardholder, for registration as a citizen of India | | 7 | VIIIA | For grant of citizenship by naturalisation | The applicant may fill up the relevant form, attach all requisite documents mentioned in the Form and make payment of fee of Rs. 50/- online. At the application stage itself, the applicant may opt for receiving the ink signed copy of the certificate of registration or certificate of naturalization. Ink signed copy of the certificate will be issued to the applicant only if he/ she has opted for the same at the application stage. In all other cases, a digital", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["about", "citizen", "documents", "faq", "frequently", "indiancitizenshiponlinenicin", "info", "procedure", "registration", "service"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_indiancitizenshiponlineni_c1794695_01", "source_url": "https://indiancitizenshiponline.nic.in/Home/IndexHI", "title": "Indian Citizenship Online - हिंदी", "section": "Overview", "text": "भारत की नागरिकता के बारे में भारतीय नागरिकता का अधिग्रहण जन्म, वंश, पंजीकरण और देशीयकरण द्वारा किया जा सकता है। नागरिकता अधिनियम, 1955 के प्रावधान के अनुसार भारतीय नागरिकता के अधिग्रहण की शर्तों और प्रक्रिया को निम्न लिंक पर पढ़ा जा सकता है:अधिग्रहण आदेश और परिपत्र ऑनलाइन सेवाएं - नागरिकता संशोधन अधिनियम (सीएए) भारतीय नागरिकता का अधिग्रहण नागरिकता संशोधन अधिनियम 2019 के तहत भारतीय नागरिकता के लिए आवेदन करने के लिए एक विशेष प्रावधान मौजूद है। यह विशेष रूप से उन कुछ व्यक्तियों के लिए है जो 31 दिसंबर, 2014 को या उससे पहले भारत में प्रवेश कर चुके हैं और पाकिस्तान या अफगानिस्तान या बांग्लादेश के हिन्दू या सिख या बौद्ध या जैन या पारसी या ईसाई समुदाय से हैं। अधिक विस्तृत जानकारी के लिए, व्यक्ति 1955 के नागरिकता अधिनियम में उल्लिखित प्रावधानों का संदर्भ ले सकते हैं। आवेदन जमा करने के इच्छुक व्यक्तियों के पास अपना ईमेल आईडी और मोबाइल नंबर होना चाहिए। आवेदक सीएए 2019 के तहत भारतीय नागरिकता के लिए आवेदन जमा करने के लिए बटन पर क्लिक कर सकते हैं और अपने व्यक्तिगत ईमेल आईडी और मोबाइल नंबर का उपयोग करके लॉग इन कर सकते हैं। सीएए के प्रावधानों को देखने के लिए आप यहां क्लिक कर सकते हैं। नागरिकता संशोधन अधिनियम (सीएए) - अक्सर पूछे जाने वाले प्रश्न नागरिकता संशोधन अधिनियम (सीएए) अक्सर पूछे जाने वाले प्रश्न - (i) जिन्होंने 31.12.2014 को या उससे पहले भारत में प्रवेश किया; और - (ii) जिसे पासपोर्ट (भारत में प्रवेश) अधिनियम, 1920 की धारा 3(2)(सी) के तहत या विदेशी अधिनियम, 1946 के प्रावधानों या उसके तहत बनाए गए किसी नियम या आदेश से छूट दी गई है। | क्रं सं. | प्रपत्र संख्या | पात्र व्यक्तियों की श्रेणी | |---|---|---| | 1 | IIA | भारत के नागरिक के रूप में पंजीकरण के लिए भारतीय मूल का व्यक्ति | | 2 | IIIA | भारत के नागरिक के रूप में पंजीकरण के लिए एक व्यक्ति जिसने भारत के नागरिक से विवाह किया है | | 3 | IVA | भारत के नागरिक के रूप में पंजीकरण के लिए वह व्यक्ति जो भारत के नागरिक हैं, की नाबालिग संतान है | | 4 | VA | भारत के नागरिक के रूप में पंजीकरण के लिए एक व्यक्ति जिसके माता-पिता भारत के नागरिक के रूप में पंजीकृत हैं | | 5 | VIA | भारत के नागरिक के रूप में पंजीकरण के लिए एक व्यक्ति जो या माता-पिता में से कोई एक स्वतंत्र भारत का नागरिक था | | 6 | VIIA | एक व्यक्ति जो भारत के प्रवासी भारतीय नागरिक कार्ड होल्डर (OCI) के रूप में पंजीकृत है, भारत के नागरिक के रूप में पंजीकरण के लिए | | 7 | VIIIA | देशीयकरण द्वारा नागरिकता प्रदान करने हेतु | आवेदक उपरोक्त संबंधित फॉर्म ऑनलाइन भर सकता है। फॉर्म में उल्लिखित सभी आवश्यक दस्तावेज संलग्न कर एवं 50/- रुपये के शुल्क का ऑनलाइन भुगतान कर सकता है। आवेदन", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["indiancitizenshiponlinenicin"], "language": "hi"}
{"id": "civic_indiancitizenshiponlineni_042f20f4_01", "source_url": "https://indiancitizenshiponline.nic.in/Renounce", "title": "Indian Citizenship Online - Declaration of Renunciation of Citizenship Under Section 8 of the Act Made by a Citizen of India", "section": "Overview", "text": "Declaration of Renunciation of Citizenship under Section 8 of the Act Made by a Citizen of India RENUNCIATION OF INDIAN CITIZENSHIP List of documents to be uploaded - Indian Passport including expired ones (Please upload both front page and bio page of the passport) - Address proof | Image Uploading Criteria | Document Uploading Criteria | | 1. Needs to upload applicant passport size photograph. | 1. Needs to upload (a) Indian Passport including expired ones (Please upload both front page and bio page of the passport (b) Address proof | | 2. Image Dimension of Photograph should be 100(Width) * 120(Hight) Pixel only. | 2. Please Scan the above documents and save in PDF format. | | 3. Ensure that the size of the scanned image are not more than 50kb. | 3. Each Document can contain multiple pages. | | 4. Uploading image should be in jpg format only. | 4. Each PDF Document should not exceed size more than 1024kb(1MB). | | 5. Use the Microsoft picture manager for resizing the image | |", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["citizen", "documents", "indiancitizenshiponlinenicin"], "language": "en"}
