L has issued the following Global e-tender for importing the following Bulk Fertilizer on Govt. Account: […] National Fertilizers Limited (NFL) National Fertilizers Limited (NFL) is a Public Sector Undertaking (PSU), a Nav-Ratna company under the Department of Fertilizers, Ministry of Chemicals and Fertilizers, Government of India. NFL has an annual Urea production capacity of 3.56 Million Tonnes and is the second largest producer of Urea in India. NFL is also engaged […] Global e-tender for Import of Urea (46:00:00) on Govt. account (E-tender ID: 2025_NFL_236730_1) National Fertilizers Limited (NFL) is a Public Sector Undertaking (PSU), a Navratna company under the Department of Fertilizers, Ministry of Chemicals and Fertilizers, Government of India. NFL has issued the following Global e-tender for importing the following Bulk Fertilizer for the Government […] Global e-Tender for Import of DAP (18:46:00) National Fertilizers Limited (NFL) is a Public Sector Undertaking (PSU), a Nav-Ratna company under the Department of Fertilizers, Ministry of Chemicals and Fertilizers, Government of India. NFL has an annual Urea production capacity of 3.56 Million Tonnes and is the second largest producer of Urea in India. NFL […] Integrity Pact Notice Inviting Tender (NIT) for Empanelment of Reputed Manufacturers & Traders for supply of Imported DAP Global", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["eoitashkentgovin", "portal"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_eoitashkentgovin_8652bf19_01", "source_url": "https://eoitashkent.gov.in/information-about-visa-services/", "title": "Embassy of India, Tashkent, Uzbekistan - Information about Visa Services", "section": "Overview", "text": "Information about Visa Services IMPORTANT INFORMATION FOR VISA APPLICANTS For Indian regular/ paper Visa, applicants are required to fill the online application according to the instructions provided at India Visa Online Applicant should fill the form for regular paper Visa at India Visa Online. It is MANDATORY to upload a latest digital photograph (as per ICAO specification). Take a printout of the filled-in form generated in pdf format, and carry two copies of the same photograph as uploaded on the online application form; - Applications without an uploaded photograph will be rejected; - A printout of the duly filled online form with the photograph must be signed by the applicant and presented in person at the Embassy, along with requisite fees and all other required documents for the visa issuance; - Presence of the applicant at the Embassy is required for the collection of Biometric Data; - A separate visa form must be filled for each child traveling with the parent, even if the child’s name is included in the parent’s passport; - The new visa stickers are issued without the signature and stamp from the Embassy. Afghan Passport holders can apply visa at India Visa Online WORKING HOURS Visa applications are to be submitted in person at the Consular Section of the Embassy of India, Tashkent: - Acceptance of Visa Applications: 09:30 – 12:30 hrs. on Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, and Friday except holidays. - Collection of Visas: 15:30 – 16:00 hrs. on the specified date. - The Embassy is closed on Saturdays, Sundays, and designated holidays. Business Visa General Information The Business Visa is granted subject to the following conditions: - The applicant must have assured financial standing and expertise in the intended business field. - The applicant must not be visiting India for money-lending, petty trading, or full-time employment with salary payment in India. - Business Visa is also extended to senior executives, experts, tour conductors, and travel agents visiting India for work related to national projects or business tours for foreigners. - The Business Visa must be issued from the applicant’s country of origin or domicile or with a residence duration of over 2 years in that country. Documents Required | Type of Visa | Purpose | Documents Required | |---|---|---| | Business Visa | Issued to persons intending to travel to India for business purposes | | Please ensure the following when submitting your Indian visa application: - Your passport must be valid for at least 6 months. - Your passport must have at least 2 blank pages. - The visa validity is effective from the date of issue. - The Embassy/Consulate reserves the right to ask for additional documents. - Submission of the application along with the prescribed fee does not guarantee issuance of the visa. Entry Visa (X – Visa) General Information | Type of Visa | Purpose | Documents Required | |---|---|---|", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["about", "apply", "documents", "eoitashkentgovin", "info", "service"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_eoitashkentgovin_a35c5bb8_01", "source_url": "https://eoitashkent.gov.in/online-filing-tracking-commercial-quality-complaints-trade-disputes/", "title": "Embassy of India, Tashkent, Uzbekistan - Online Filing & Tracking Commercial Quality Complaints/ Trade Disputes", "section": "Overview", "text": "Online Filing & Tracking Commercial Quality Complaints/ Trade Disputes Guidelines for the Complainants - Go to DGFT website www.dgft.gov.in > Quick Links > File Quality/ Trade Grievances > fill Online Application Form. (http://dgftebrc.nic.in:8090/TradeDispute/) - Upload documents related to the quality complaint/trade dispute, wherever required (maximum 5 MB size documents in pdf format). - Submit Online Application Form to the jurisdictional RA of DGFT / SEZ (this jurisdiction should be ascertained by the complainant, with respect to the Indian entity against whom the complaint is being made or with respect to the Indian complainant where the complaint is being filed against a foreign entity, as per Appendix of Handbook of Procedures (https://dgft.gov.in/sites/default/files/1A_0.pdf)). - On submission, a Unique Reference Number (URN) starting with ‘Q’ will be generated and sent to the email id of the complainant. Please make sure that the email id is functional as all future correspondence will be made on this id only. - The complainant, at a future date, can also provide additional material/ correspondence to the DGFT RA/ SEZ. While making any future correspondence with the DGFT RA/ SEZ to whom the Online Application has been submitted earlier, the URN must be quoted invariably in the subject header of the email. - A link ‘View Status’ is also available for the complainant to check current position of the complaint at http://dgftebrc.nic.in:8090/TradeDispute/status.", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["documents", "eoitashkentgovin", "grievance", "guideline", "procedure", "status", "track"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_eoitashkentgovin_b8259ce5_01", "source_url": "https://eoitashkent.gov.in/mandatory-uploading-of-icao-compliant-photographs-for-availing-passport-services/", "title": "Mandatory uploading of ICAO compliant photographs for availing passport services - Embassy of India, Tashkent", "section": "Overview", "text": "Mandatory uploading of ICAO compliant photographs for availing passport services On induction of the new Global Passport Seva Version 2.0, Indian passport holders applying for renewal of passports at the Embassy of India, Tashkent are required to mandatorily upload ICAO-compliant photographs while filling out the application. Detailed guidelines for ICAO-compliant photographs for passport applications and the SOP for applicants are given below:", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["apply", "eoitashkentgovin", "guideline", "service"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_cgisaopaulogovin_15b49739_01", "source_url": "https://www.cgisaopaulo.gov.in/index.php", "title": "Consulate General of India, Sao Paulo, Brazil", "section": "Overview", "text": "The Consulate General of India, SÃ£o Paulo along with members of Indian diaspora and friends of India enthusiastically celebrated the 80th Independence Day with patriotic fervour and spirit of unity and National pride. Consul General Hansraj Singh Verma led a curated Yoga session at the iconic Ipiranga Museum, SÃ£o Paulo, bringing together more than 250 yoga enthusiasts from across the city. Consul General Mr. Hansraj Singh Verma inaugurated the Indian Pavilion at FEIMEC 2026, Brazil's largest machinery trade fair being held at Sao Paulo from 5th to 9th May 2026. Glimpses of National Day reception hosted by the Consulate General of India (26.01.2026). Consul General Shri Hansraj Singh Verma unfurled the Indian National Flag on the occasion of the 77th Republic Day of India. Members of the Indian community and friends of India joined the celebrations with great enthusiasm. Consul General Hansraj Singh Verma joined the World Hindi Day 2026 celebrations at SVCC SÃ£o Paulo on 09.01.2026. Members of the Indian community and students of SVCC, Sao Paulo took part in Hindi competitions, winning exciting prizes, followed by a Hindi film screening, promoting the Hindi language in Brazil. Ambassador Dinesh Bhatia presented trade & economic opportunities between India & Brazil at a business meeting hosted by LIDE in Sao Paulo. Ambassador Dinesh Bhatia gave keynote address at \"Tourism through Culture\" event by ICCR, Sao Paulo, attended by over 40 Brazilian travel agencies and included a classical dance to commemorate 150 years of Vande Mataram. Ambassador Mr. Dinesh Bhatia and Mrs. Seema Bhatia hosted Diwali celebrations for Indian community & Brazilian friends of India in Sao Paulo. Consul General of India Shri Hansraj Singh Verma joined by Indian community & friends of India, hoisted the national flag on the occasion of India's 79th Independence Day (15 August 2025). Ambassador of India to Brazil Dinesh Bhatia interacts with the Indian business community in Sao Paulo. Consul General Hansraj Singh Verma visited the newly opened SÃ£o Paulo branch of India Exim Bank. Ambassador Dinesh Bhatia & Mrs. Seema Bhatia and Consul General Hansraj Singh Verma & Mrs. Kalpana Hansraj had the honour of welcoming Hon'ble Prime Minister Narendra Modi upon his arrival in Rio de Janeiro for the 17th BRICS Summit. President Lula warmly receive PM Narendra Modi at Alvorada Palace in Brasilia. Prime Minister Narendra Modi alongside other BRICS leaders at the Summit held in Rio de Janeiro, Brazil. Welcome to the Consulate General of India, Sao Paulo, Brazil The States of SÃ£o Paulo, Rio de Janeiro, ParanÃ¡, Santa Catarina and Rio Grande do Sul fall under the jurisdiction of this Consulate. Residents of all other states in Brazil may obtain information and services from theÂ Embassy of India, Brasilia.Â (Website:Â http://www.eoibrasilia.gov.in/Â ) A Ãndia implementou requisitos de entrada relacionados Ã vacina contra a Febre Amarela, conforme o Regulamento SanitÃ¡rio Internacional (RSI) de 2005. De acordo com o RSI, viajantes com mais", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["acts", "cgisaopaulogovin", "info", "service"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_cgisaopaulogovin_f05481bc_01", "source_url": "https://www.cgisaopaulo.gov.in/passported-services.php", "title": "Consulate General of India, Sao Paulo, Brazil - Documents Required", "section": "Overview", "text": "Important Notice regarding passport applications. Guidelines for ICAO Compliant Photographs for Passport Applications. General Instructions for Passport Services (Please see below for Portuguese Translation) Jurisdiction Consulate General of India Sao Paulo issues regular paper visa service only to those who are resident in its consular jurisdiction, that is, those residing in any of the five states of Brazil viz Sao Paulo, Rio de Janeiro, Parana, Santa Catarina or Rio Grande do Sul. The other states may apply to Embassy of India in Brasilia. The applicants are specifically requested to ensure before submitting or sending documents by Post that they have appended their signature and photograph on the application form, furnished correct and mandatory details, the requisite supportive documents, English translation of Portuguese or other foreign language documents. Incomplete application or applications with incomplete details will be summarily rejected and no representation will be entertained in this regard. The timings of Passport Services are as under: (Monday to Friday) 0930-1200 hrs. - Acceptance of Passport applications 1500-1600 hrs. – Delivery of New Passport 0900-1730 hrs - By Sedex (Monday to Friday) Please read instructions carefully before you start the application process. 1) A new Indian Passports are now normally issued with a validity of 10 years (except in the case of children up to the age of 15 years where it is issued for a validity of 5 years). Their re-issue thereafter involves the issuance of a new Passport. A new Passport needs to be obtained as the practice of handwritten endorsements in the existing Passport has been done away with. 2) When new booklet is necessitated on account of change in basic particulars like name, appearance and when all pages have been exhausted. 3) A new Passport can be issued one year before final expiry or on final expiry of any Passport issued for full validity of 10 years (5 years in the case of minors). Children’s names are no longer entered in their parent’s Passport. 4) Applications for Passport Services can be submitted and collected either in person or by post. If, due to any reason, an applicant is not in a position to apply/collect in person, only a close family member(spouse or blood relative) can apply/collect on behalf of an applicant with a proper authority letter. The close family member will be required to produce this authority letter and his/her original passport/identity paper/document establishing the proof of his/her relationship with the applicant while submitting the application on behalf of the applicant. 5) It is an offence under the Passports Act, 1967 to knowingly furnish false information or to suppress material information when applying for Passport Services. 6) If you observe printing mistake in your newly issued Passport, please contact the Passport Counters immediately. If it is a mistake by the Passport Section, the correction (s) will be made immediately without charging any fee to correct the mistake. If", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["apply", "cgisaopaulogovin", "contact", "documents", "guideline", "info", "process", "service"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_cgisaopaulogovin_efc0ccb9_01", "source_url": "https://www.cgisaopaulo.gov.in/misc-service-through-sewa-portal.php", "title": "Consulate General of India, Sao Paulo, Brazil - Miscellaneous Services through SEWA Portal", "section": "Overview", "text": "MISCELLANEOUS CONSULAR SERVICES Consulate General of India, SÃ£o Paulo All Miscellaneous Consular Services must be applied online through the SEWA Portal: https://indianconsularservices.mea.gov.in/consularServices/ Applicants are requested to carefully follow the steps mentioned below: Step 1: Registration / Login Visit the SEWA portal: https://indianconsularservices.mea.gov.in/consularServices/ New users must register on the portal by creating a User ID and password using their email address. After successful registration, login to the portal using the registered credentials. Step 2: Apply for the Required Service - After logging in, choose the required service from the list of services. - Fill in the online application form with the correct personal details. - Upload the required supporting documents as specified for the selected service. - Review the details carefully and submit the application online. Step 3: Verification of Application - The Consulate will verify the application and documents submitted online. - Applicants will receive a notification on the portal regarding the status of the application. - If any discrepancy or additional document is required, the same will be communicated through the portal. - Applicants must upload the correct documents and re-submit the application online. Step 4: Submission of Documents at the Consulate Once the application is approved/verified online, the applicant must print the completed application form from the portal. - Visit the Consulate with: - Printed and signed application form - One set of photocopies of all uploaded documents - Original documents for verification Applications can be submitted in person at: Consulate General of India Av. Paulista, 925 â 7th Floor Bela Vista, SÃ£o Paulo â SP CEP: 01311-100 Submission Timing: Monday to Friday (excluding public holidays) 09:30 AM â 12:00 PM Where applicable, applications may also be sent by post (SEDEX) along with the required documents. Step 5: Collection of Processed Documents After processing, the ready document can be collected from the Consulate on any working day between 03:00 PM â 04:00 PM. If the applicant has provided a return SEDEX envelope and submitted the SEDEX fee of R$ 82, the processed document may also be sent by post. Miscellaneous Consular Services Available through SEWA Portal - Attestation of Civil Documents - Attestation of Commercial Documents - Attestation of Educational Documents - Attestation of General Documents (Passport, Bank Statement, Driving Licence, etc.) - Attestation of Personal Documents - Attestation of Power of Attorney - Birth Certificate â Child - Birth Certificate â Self - NRI Certificate â Educational Purpose - Registration of Child Birth - Registration of Marriage, etc. - Police Clearance Certificate (for OCI Cardholders/Foreign Citizens) Important Notes: Applicants are advised to visit/send documents to the Consulate only after receiving confirmation of verification/approval on the SEWA portal. - No prior appointment is required for submission or collection of documents. Applicants should ensure that all documents uploaded online are clear and legible to avoid delays in processing. Last Updated: March 2026", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["apply", "cgisaopaulogovin", "citizen", "documents", "portal", "process", "registration", "service", "status", "verify"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_cgisaopaulogovin_51293696_01", "source_url": "https://www.cgisaopaulo.gov.in/guidelines%20for%20applicants%20for%20registering%20grievance.php", "title": "Consulate General of India, Sao Paulo, Brazil - Guidelines for Applicants for Registering Grievance", "section": "Overview", "text": "Guidelines for applicants for registering grievance Ministry of External Affairs Indian Missions/Posts attach great importance to speedy redressal of consular grievances of Indians in distress abroad and to provide them necessary assistance. Being diplomatic entities, however, it is obligatory on the part of our Missions/Posts, to conform to the established international norms of engagement in a foreign country with the host government authorities, foreign private establishments and private individuals. There could be issues and situations, where an intervention by our Missions/Posts may not be considered desirable. It is, thus, advisable to familiarize oneself with the local norms and regulations as this may be helpful in avoiding/handling certain issues obviating the need for registering a grievance with the Indian Mission/Post. The applicants are advised to go through the following basic guidelines before registering their grievances on MADAD/CPGRAM portal, approaching an Indian embassy/consulate or Ministry of External Affairs (Consular, Passport & Visa, Overseas Employment & Protector General of Emigrants, Overseas Indian Affairs I & II Divisions) : (i) The MADAD/CPGRAM portals are for filing grievances by Indian nationals only. Foreigners may submit their grievance to the Community Welfare/Consular Section in the concerned Indian Mission/Post through e-mail. (ii) In matters like; purely family disputes, seeking help of Indian authorities in resolving issues in India, complaints with foreign airlines/private school abroad etc., applicants are advised to approach the concerned authority in India/abroad. (iii) For demand of action against a foreign entity/individuals, the complainant should approach the concerned authority of the foreign country. The Ministry of External Affairs or Indian Missions/Posts cannot initiate punitive action against Indian nationals (such as revocation/impounding/cancellation of passports) based on complaints by individuals; Orders from Court/legal basis, is required for such action. It is beyond the purview of the Ministry of External Affairs/Indian Missions/Posts to prevent individuals from leaving/entering India or other countries or intervene in the process of grant of foreign visas. (iv) The personal issues in marital relationships fall beyond the ambit of consular grievance. Indian Missions/Posts would, however, readily assist destitute Indian nationals abroad, particularly women in distress and children, on case to case basis. (v) For commercial disputes, the portal of the Director General of Foreign Trade at https://www.dgft.gov.in/CP/?opt=quality-compaints may first be approached. (vi) For Queries related to foreign private entities (which are not under the control of Government of India) such as International Indian Schools abroad, individual should approach the concerned authority in foreign country. (vii) Requests to file court cases in a foreign country/India on behalf of an individual may not be possible for Indian Embassies/Consulates as diplomatic entities. (viii) Complaints against fraud (including online fraud) or any criminal activities, are required to be filed with the law enforcement agency concerned. Filing a complaint with Indian Missions/Posts is not sufficient in such cases. (ix) Grievances pertaining to employment related issues may be filed. Indian Missions/Posts attempt reconciliation through negotiation, where both parties agree. It", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["cgisaopaulogovin", "grievance", "guideline", "help", "portal", "process"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_cgisaopaulogovin_dc3657c9_01", "source_url": "https://www.cgisaopaulo.gov.in/Right-to-Information.php", "title": "Consulate General of India, Sao Paulo, Brazil - Right to Information", "section": "Overview", "text": "RIGHT TO INFORMATION The Right to Information under the provisions of the RTI Act is available to the citizens of India only. RTI Act is an important legislation designed to promote transparency and accountability in the functioning of public authorities. The full text of the RTI Act is available on the website: RTI-Act.pdf. The RTI Act also provides for appeals by aggrieved persons to the Central Information Commission of the Government of India. Indian citizens resident in States of São Paulo, Rio de Janeiro, Parana, Santa Catarina and Rio Grande do Sul may seek information in writing on payment of requisite fee during office hours on working days as per procedure laid down in the RTI Act, 2005. Contact details of officers for addressing applications under Right to Information Act, 2005: Chief Public Information Officer Shri Rajesh Kumar Vice Consul (Admin/Accts/RTI) Phone: +55 11 9764554967 E-mail: admn.saopaulo@mea.gov.in Appellate Authority Shri Preetham S. Consul Phone: + 55 11 33279 3770 Email: com.saopaulo@mea.gov.in Applications seeking information under the Act may be sent along with a fee in Brazilian Real equivalent to INR 10/- (Indian Rupee ten only) in cheque or demand draft favoring Consulate General of India. It may be noted that information provided under the Act is available to citizens of India only. Applications should be submitted along with documentary proof of Indian Citizenship (like copy of personal particulars pages of passport). More information is available at http://rti.gov.in. The mailing address is Av. Paulista, 925, 7th Floor, Bela Vista, Sao Paulo (Brazil). CEP 01311-100. It may also be pointed out that as per section 6(1) (a) of the RTI Act, 2005, a person who desires to obtain information under the Act is required to submit the application to the Information Officer of the “concerned public authority”. Applicants are, therefore, advised to send their requests under the RTI Act to the Embassy only when the subject matter can reasonably be presumed to pertain to the Embassy. While section 6 (3) provides for the transfer of an application by a receiving PIO to another [concerned] PIO, this is clearly meant to cover situations where the application is addressed to a PIO on the assumption that it has been directed to the concerned PIO. Where the information required obviously does not pertain to the Embassy, the application may be addressed to the concerned PIO directly. Payment of RTI fee online - Electronic Indian Postal Order (eIPO) The scheme of Electronic Indian Postal Order (eIPO) has been launched by the Department of Posts, Ministry of Communications and Information Technology, in association with Department of Personnel and Training (DoPT). This would enable the Indian citizens abroad to pay the RTI fee online. An Indian Postal Order can be purchased electronically by paying a fee on-line through e-Post Office Portal or through India Post website. The web-links for payment are: www.indiapost.gov.in www.epostoffice.gov.in The Credit Card or Debit", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["cgisaopaulogovin", "citizen", "contact", "info", "portal", "procedure", "scheme"], "language": "en"}
