s the gathering during the special event to mark Hindi Pakhwada-2026- 25.09.2026 September 23, 2026 Ambassadors interaction with key functionaries of prominent Ayurveda and wellbeing resorts in Azerbaijan-23.09.2026 September 23, 2026 Ambassador adresses the gathering during the Great Indian Ayurveda Festival-23.09.2026 September 23, 2026 Ambassador adresses the gathering during the Great Indian Ayurveda Festival-2-23.09.2026 August 20, 2026 Ambassador met the Chairman and student members of the Writers’ Club of Azerbaijan University of Languages-20.09.2026 September 18, 2026 Glimpses from the Hindi Diwas event at the Chancery on 18.09.2026 September 18, 2026 Opening of Permanent Exhibition on UNESCO World Heritage Sites of India-18.07.2026 September 18, 2026 Ambassador adresses the particiapants at the special event to mark the Hindi Diwas at the Chancery- 18.09.2026 September 17, 2026 Ambassador leads the Swachta hi Seva and Ek Ped Maa ke naam initiative at the Chancery-1-17.09.2026", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["indianembassybakugovin"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_indianembassybakugovin_400d61b2_01", "source_url": "https://www.indianembassybaku.gov.in/page/overseas-citizen-of-india-oci-scheme/", "title": "Overseas Citizen of India (OCI) Scheme | Embassy of India, Baku, Azerbaijan", "section": "Overview", "text": "Embassy of India Baku ***** NOTICE The Government of India has launched electronic Overseas Citizen of India (e-OCI) Cards in lieu of physical OCI cards for the new applicants and existing OCI card holding physical booklets. The following are the useful points with regard to e-OCI cards : a) e-OCI card has been launched on 30.06.2026 for the new applicants and existing OCI card holding physical booklets. b) The new e-OCI card incorporates enhanced security features and has been integrated with all the Immigration Check Posts (ICPs). c) The holder of e-OCI card will need not carry the physical copy of the OCI card at the time of Immigration Clearance and for availing other services. d) The e-OCI card can be downloaded by login into OCI portal (https://ociservices.gov.in ) and through the official ‘Indian Visa Su Swagatam” mobile app. e) The physical booklets shall continue to remain valid and shall be accepted for immigration and other associated services. It is informed that now onwards, only digital OCI card (e-OCI) will be issued to all new OCI applicants as well as existing physical booklet OCI Card holders. *****", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["citizen", "download", "indianembassybakugovin", "info", "portal", "service"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_indianembassybakugovin_90746c0d_01", "source_url": "https://www.indianembassybaku.gov.in/page/right-to-information-rti/", "title": "Right to Information RTI | Embassy of India, Baku, Azerbaijan", "section": "Overview", "text": "RIGHT TO INFORMATION The Right to Information under the provisions of the RTI Act 2005 is available to the citizens of India only. RTI Act 2005 is an important legislation designed to promote transparency and accountability in the functioning of public authorities. The full text of the RTI Act 2005 is available on the website: RTI-Act.pdf. The RTI Act also provides for appeals by aggrieved persons to the Central Information Commission of the Government of India. Indian citizens resident in Azerbaijan may seek information in writing on payment of requisite fee during office hours on working days as per procedure laid down in the RTI Act, 2005. Contact details of officers for addressing applications under Right to Information Act, 2005: Central Public Information Officer Shri Sanjay Bishnoi Attache(Admin) & CPIO Email: admin[dot]baku[at]mea[dot]gov[dot]in Appellate Authority Mr. Sanjay Jain Counsellor Email: hoc[dot]baku[at]mea[dot]gov[dot]in Fees for RTI Application - Applications seeking information under the Act may be sent along with a fee in Azerbaijani Manat equivalent to INR 10/- (Indian Rupee ten only) by cash at the Embassy. It may be noted that information provided under the Act is available to citizens of India only. Applications should be submitted along with documentary proof of Indian Citizenship (like copy of personal particulars pages of passport). More information is available at http://rti.gov.in. The mailing address is Embassy of India, Baku, 6A Olimpia Street, Ganjlik, Narimanov District, Baku AZ1072, Azerbaijan. It may also be pointed out that as per section 6(1) (a) of the RTI Act, 2005, a person who desires to obtain information under the Act is required to submit the application to the Information Officer of the “concerned public authority”. Applicants are, therefore, advised to send their requests under the RTI Act to the Embassy only when the subject matter can reasonably be presumed to pertain to the Embassy. While section 6 (3) provides for the transfer of an application by a receiving PIO to another [concerned] PIO, this is clearly meant to cover situations where the application is addressed to a PIO on the assumption that it has been directed to the concerned PIO. Where the information required obviously does not pertain to the Embassy, the application may be addressed to the concerned PIO directly. Payment of RTI fee online - Electronic Indian Postal Order (eIPO) The scheme of Electronic Indian Postal Order (eIPO) has been launched by the Department of Posts, Ministry of Communications and Information Technology, in association with Department of Personnel and Training (DoPT). This would enable the Indian citizens abroad to pay the RTI fee online. An Indian Postal Order can be purchased electronically by paying a fee on-line through e-Post Office Portal or through India Post website. The web-links for payment are: www.indiapost.gov.in www.epostoffice.gov.in The Credit Card or Debit Card of any bank powered by Visa/ Master can be used for this purpose. Procedure The RTI applicant is required", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["citizen", "contact", "indianembassybakugovin", "info", "portal", "procedure", "scheme"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_indianembassybakugovin_6d6eb0ad_01", "source_url": "https://www.indianembassybaku.gov.in/page-links/", "title": "Embassy of India, Baku, Azerbaijan - Consular Services", "section": "Overview", "text": "| Embassy of India, Baku, Azerbaijan Embassy of India, Baku, Azerbaijan Embassy of India Baku, Azerbaijan What's New Home The Embassy Ambassador Working Hours Former Ambassadors Embassy Officials List of Holidays Right to Information RTI Consular Services Visa Services Regular Visa Passport Services Overseas Citizen of India (OCI) Scheme Miscellaneous Services Fee Schedule of Consular Services Application Forms Indian Community in Azerbaijan. Registration of Indian Nationals FAQ on Marital disputes involving NRI/PIO spouses Advisories for Indian Nationals Citizens Corner Bilateral Relations Fact Sheet on Azerbaijan Bilateral Brief Educational Opportunities in India and Cultural Links Cultural Exchanges Indian Technical and Economic Cooperation (ITEC) Indian Community in Azerbaijan CUSTOMS AND OTHER REGULATIONS FOR ENTRY INTO INDIA Trade Enquiry form Business / Investment Economic and Commercial Brief Doing Business in India Media Room News Announcements / Public Advisories / Updates Events/Photo Gallery Press Release Tenders Useful Links Advisories Tagore Nizami Library Contact Contact Us Feedback Location Guide for the Embassy Home Sitemap Contact Feedback Right to Information Tenders Stay Connected with MEA : Copyright Policy Hyperlinking Policy Help Website content managed by Jadon Webtech Pvt Ltd Visitors: 156853 Page last updated on: October 23, 2026 Designed & developed by Jadon Webtech Pvt Ltd Chat with us! Go to Navigation", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["citizen", "contact", "faq", "help", "indianembassybakugovin", "info", "registration", "scheme", "service"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_indianembassybakugovin_abf0df9c_01", "source_url": "https://www.indianembassybaku.gov.in/page/passport-services/", "title": "Passport Services | Embassy of India, Baku, Azerbaijan", "section": "Overview", "text": "Applications for Passport and consular services can be made at the Consular Section of the Embassy, which is open from 09:30 hours to 12:30 hours on Monday-Friday except Holidays (see List of Holidays). Passports, after completion of the service requested, can be collected from 15:30 and 17:00 hours on the date indicated. Fees for passport services are accepted at the Embassy in cash in AZN only [see fees Schedule ]. Important Notice: From September 1, 2025, only ICAO complaint photographs will be accepted for submission of passport applications. click here for ICAO guidelines. Application forms can be filled online at this link: https://mportal.passportindia.gov.in/mission/embassy For any clarification or further information, please call (012 564 6344/ 012 564 6354) or e-mail at cons[dot]baku[at]mea[dot]gov[dot]in. Your passport is a valuable document. It should always be either in your custody or in the custody of a person duly authorized by you. It must not be altered or mutilated in any way. If you have acquired foreign citizenship, please surrender the Indian passport to the nearest Indian Mission. In accordance with International Civil Aviation Organization (ICAO) guidelines, Government of India has introduced Machine Readable Passports (MRP) in all passports office in India and Embassies abroad. The Embassy of India, Baku is also participating in a centralized project operated by Ministry of External Affairs (CPV division) for issuing machine readable passports with effect from August 26, 2007. Passports are now being printed in India and couriered to the Embassy. It would require around fifteen working days* after due processing of application to issue the passport by the Embassy to the applicant. The passport seeking applicants are hereby advised to check their passport's status and apply for any passport services much in advance. New Passport on Final Expiry The hard copy of duly filled in online application form is to be submitted along with 4 photographs and the old passport along with a photocopy of the first and last page of the passport. Photographs should be of size 4 cm X 4 Cm and signatures should be inside the box given for the purpose in form. For more information about the photograph details please go through Photo-Specf 1 , 2 Applications for new passport can be submitted within one year before the final expiry of the current passport or if the only 2 pages are left in the applicant's passport. Applicant has the option to apply for an ordinary passport booklet of 36 pages or a Jumbo passport booklet of 60 pages Time Taken: * Duplicate Passport in lieu of lost/damaged passport If the passport is lost, the matter should immediately be reported to the nearest local police authorities and a proper police report regarding the loss of passport should be obtained and thereafter Embassy should be approached. If you are on a short visit to Baku and have lost or damaged your original passport you can approach", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["about", "apply", "citizen", "guideline", "indianembassybakugovin", "info", "portal", "process", "service", "status"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_incredibleindiaorg_ddbe0d6f_01", "source_url": "https://www.incredibleindia.gov.in/en", "title": "Discover Incredible India: Travel Guide & Tourism Info | Incredible India", "section": "Overview", "text": "DESTINATIONS for every bucket list Delhi The Beating Retreat Ceremony at the Attari-Wagah border is a unique ceremony that features a synchronised parade by Indian and Pakistani soldiers. Amritsar holds a significant place as a hub for Sikh martial arts, a tradition known as Gatka. Amritsar Leh is one of the highest permanently inhabited places on the planet. Leh was once a vital stop on the ancient Silk Road, connecting India to Central Asia and China. Leh Srinagar Manali Chandigarh, a union territory with its own administration, serves as the capital for two Indian states - Punjab and Haryana! The Capitol Complex, a UNESCO World Heritage site, is the epicentre of Chandigarh's administrative and political activities. Chandigarh Gurgram is home to more than 250 Fortune 500 companies. Gurugram has a link with Indian epic 'Mahabharata'. It is believed to be the village of guru Dronacharya and was called guru-gramam (guru's village). Gurugram Udaipur Haridwar is home to the world-famous Kumbh Mela. Haridwar is known for its Ayurvedic medicine and wellness centres. Haridwar Varanasi Bhubaneswar Sri Vijaya Puram Darjeeling's ‘Toy Train’ is the first and only steam-powered rack-and-pinion railway in India and one of the oldest mountain railways in the world. Over 80 operational tea gardens in Darjeeling produce the renowned Darjeeling Tea, also known as the \"Champagne of tea.\" Darjeeling Patna was the capital of the ancient Magadha kingdom and one of the most important cities of ancient India. Patna A UNESCO World Heritage Site, Old Goa is home to several historic churches and cathedrals with Portuguese influence. Goa Mumbai is the centre of the Indian film industry, often referred to as Bollywood, producing more films per year than Hollywood. Mumbai Over 5000-year-old, Gangeshwar Mahadev Temple is believed to be built by Pandavas during their exile. Diu Dwarka Indore has held the title of India's cleanest city for six consecutive years, from 2017 to 2022. The gates of Lalbagh Palace in Indore are replicas of those found at Buckingham Palace in London. Cast in England, they were then transported to Indore. Indore Urja Park in Raipur is a unique destination designed to educate visitors on the generation and use of various forms of renewable energy sources! Raipur The Tropic of Cancer passes through Ranchi at 23.4 degrees north, making it one of the few cities in the world to be situated precisely on a major latitude. Ranchi is often called the \"City of Waterfalls\" because of the numerous waterfalls nearby, including the Hundru, Jonha, and Dassam Falls. Ranchi Ramoji Film City is the largest film studio in the world. Hyderabad Hampi Kavaratti is home to the Laccadive Sea swallow, also known as the swiftlet or edible-nest swiftlet. Kavaratti serves as the administrative capital of the Union Territory of Lakshadweep and holds the distinction of being the smallest island capital in India. Kavaratti An average of more than 2.8 lakh Tirupati", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["incredibleindiaorg"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_incredibleindiaorg_3c6f185e_01", "source_url": "https://www.incredibleindia.gov.in/en/faqs", "title": "FAQs", "section": "Overview", "text": "Essential traveler information Prepare for an enriching adventure in India with our comprehensive travel guide. From essential travel documents to diverse accommodations and top travel itineraries, we've got you covered. Get ready for an unforgettable experience in India! Explore India with confidence using our travel guide. Learn about transportation modes, booking options, safety tips, and more. From reliable local transport to scenic train routes, we've got you covered. Get ready for an unforgettable adventure! This FAQ section offers essential insights into managing your finances, understanding average expenses, and ensuring a secure and authentic shopping experience while exploring the vibrant diversity of India. Embark on a journey through our meticulously curated FAQ section, designed to offer invaluable insights into language nuances, communication decorum, and optimal connectivity solutions. These tailored resources are crafted to facilitate a seamless exploration of India's diverse and captivating landscapes. Discover indispensable tips for seamless dining experiences, respectful interactions, and immersive cultural engagements. This guide is tailored to empower you during your Indian adventure. Discover insights on healthcare accessibility, language considerations, and engaging activities for every season - this is your guide to making the most of your Indian excursion, providing valuable tips and resources tailored to your needs. Frequently asked questions Explore frequently asked questions about visiting India. - All foreign visitors need a visa, expect citizens of Nepal and Bhutan. Visa-on-Arrival facility is available to the citizens of Japan, South Korea & UAE (only for such UAE nationals who had earlier obtained e-Visa or regular/paper visa for India). Others can apply online at https://indianvisaonline.gov.in. - Minimum six months of validity and two blank pages for the Immigration stamps. Note that the visa validity starts from the issue date. - Persons arriving from Yellow Fever endemic countries or those who have visited such countries during the past 6 days immediately preceding their entry into India will be required to possess a valid certificate of Yellow Fever vaccination from an authorized vaccination centre. Persons arriving from a country having public health risk may be required to undergo medical screening or additional measures as decided by Ministry of Health and Family Welfare of India. Frequently asked questions Explore frequently asked questions about visiting India. - Air, Rail and Road are the main transportation modes in India. To book your travel, you can use various mobile applications and online websites including irctc.co.in, the website of the Indian Railway Catering and Tourism Corporation. You can also contact authorized tour operators / travel agents. - Yes, you can rent a vehicle in India. Foreigner visitors with a valid international driving permit / license can drive in India during their stay. Frequently asked questions Explore frequently asked questions about visiting India. - The Indian currency is called the Indian Rupee (INR) and one can exchange foreign currency at the airports, hotels, Reserve Bank of India approved money changers and selected local banks. -", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["about", "apply", "citizen", "contact", "documents", "faq", "frequently", "incredibleindiaorg", "info"], "language": "en"}
