{"id": "civic_aranyagovin_d1672a6a_01", "source_url": "https://aranya.gov.in/aranyacms/(S(dyxobhfg1nrhnsxgfvdkxjgx))/Kannada/EServiceKannada.aspx", "title": "Karnataka Forest Department - ಇ-ಉಪಕ್ರಮಗಳು", "section": "Overview", "text": "ಇ-ಸಸ್ಯಕ್ಷೇತ್ರ ಲಿಂಕ್ಗೆ ಹೋಗಿ >> ಇನ್ನಷ್ಟು ತಿಳಿಯಿರಿ ಇ-ಮೌಲ್ಯಮಾಪನ ಲಿಂಕ್ಗೆ ಹೋಗಿ >> ಇನ್ನಷ್ಟು ತಿಳಿಯಿರಿ ಮೌಲ್ಯಮಾಪನ ಎಪಿಓ ಲಿಂಕ್ಗೆ ಹೋಗಿ >> ಇನ್ನಷ್ಟು ತಿಳಿಯಿರಿ ಅರಣ್ಯ ಉತ್ಪನ್ನ ಟ್ರ್ಯಾಕಿಂಗ್ ವ್ಯವಸ್ಥೆ ಲಿಂಕ್ಗೆ ಹೋಗಿ >> ಇನ್ನಷ್ಟು ತಿಳಿಯಿರಿ ಇ-ಕಟಾವಣೆ ಲಿಂಕ್ಗೆ ಹೋಗಿ >> ಇನ್ನಷ್ಟು ತಿಳಿಯಿರಿ ಇ-ಟಿಂಬರ್ ಲಿಂಕ್ಗೆ ಹೋಗಿ >> ಇನ್ನಷ್ಟು ತಿಳಿಯಿರಿ ಇ-ಪರಿಹಾರ ಲಿಂಕ್ಗೆ ಹೋಗಿ >> ಇನ್ನಷ್ಟು ತಿಳಿಯಿರಿ ಇ-ಪ್ರಹರಿ ಲಿಂಕ್ಗೆ ಹೋಗಿ >> ಇನ್ನಷ್ಟು ತಿಳಿಯಿರಿ ಅನುಮೋದಿತ ಎಫ್ಸಿ ಪ್ರಕರಣಗಳು: ಷರತ್ತುಪಾಲನೆ ನಿಗಾ ವ್ಯವಸ್ಥೆ ಲಿಂಕ್ಗೆ ಹೋಗಿ >> ಇನ್ನಷ್ಟು ತಿಳಿಯಿರಿ ಬಾಕಿ ಇರುವ ಎಫ್ಸಿ ಪ್ರಕರಣಗಳ ಟ್ರ್ಯಾಕಿಂಗ್ ವ್ಯವಸ್ಥೆ ಲಿಂಕ್ಗೆ ಹೋಗಿ >> ಇನ್ನಷ್ಟು ತಿಳಿಯಿರಿ ಆಯವ್ಯಯ ನಿಗಾ ವ್ಯವಸ್ಥೆ ಲಿಂಕ್ಗೆ ಹೋಗಿ >> ಇನ್ನಷ್ಟು ತಿಳಿಯಿರಿ ಅರಣ್ಯ ಇಲಾಖೆಯ ಭೌಗೋಳಿಕ ಮಾಹಿತಿ ವ್ಯವಸ್ಥೆ ಲಿಂಕ್ಗೆ ಹೋಗಿ >> ಇನ್ನಷ್ಟು ತಿಳಿಯಿರಿ ಹೆಚ್ ಆರ್ ದತ್ತಾಂಶ ಲಿಂಕ್ಗೆ ಹೋಗಿ >> ಇನ್ನಷ್ಟು ತಿಳಿಯಿರಿ ಅರಣ್ಯ ಸ್ವತ್ತು ನಿರ್ವಹಣಾ ವ್ಯವಸ್ಥೆ ಲಿಂಕ್ಗೆ ಹೋಗಿ >> ಇನ್ನಷ್ಟು ತಿಳಿಯಿರಿ ಸಾಮಿಲ್ ನಿರ್ವಹಣೆ ವ್ಯವಸ್ಥೆ ಲಿಂಕ್ಗೆ ಹೋಗಿ >> ಇನ್ನಷ್ಟು ತಿಳಿಯಿರಿ KSFSM-2025 ಲಿಂಕ್ಗೆ ಹೋಗಿ >> ಇನ್ನಷ್ಟು ತಿಳಿಯಿರಿ ಗರುಡಾಕ್ಷಿ ಲಿಂಕ್ಗೆ ಹೋಗಿ >> ಇನ್ನಷ್ಟು ತಿಳಿಯಿರಿ ವನ್ಯಜೀವಿ ಮುಂಜಾಗ್ರತಾ ಎಚ್ಚರಿಕೆ ಸಂದೇಶ ವ್ಯವಸ್ಥೆ ಲಿಂಕ್ಗೆ ಹೋಗಿ >> ಇನ್ನಷ್ಟು ತಿಳಿಯಿರಿ ಫೋರೆಸ್ಟ್ ಕವರ್ ಮ್ಯಾಪಿಂಗ್ (ಪಿಸಿಎಂ) ಲಿಂಕ್ಗೆ ಹೋಗಿ >> ಇನ್ನಷ್ಟು ತಿಳಿಯಿರಿ ಅರಣ್ಯ ವಿಹಾರ ಲಿಂಕ್ಗೆ ಹೋಗಿ >> ಇನ್ನಷ್ಟು ತಿಳಿಯಿರಿ ಕ್ರಮ ಕೈಗೊಂಡ ವರದಿ ಮೇಲ್ವಿಚಾರಣಾ ವ್ಯವಸ್ಥೆ ಲಿಂಕ್ಗೆ ಹೋಗಿ >> ಇನ್ನಷ್ಟು ತಿಳಿಯಿರಿ ಅರಣ್ಯ ಸ್ಪಂದನ ಲಿಂಕ್ಗೆ ಹೋಗಿ >> ಇನ್ನಷ್ಟು ತಿಳಿಯಿರಿ ಇ-ಗ್ರೀನ್ವಾಚ್ ಲಿಂಕ್ಗೆ ಹೋಗಿ >> ಇನ್ನಷ್ಟು ತಿಳಿಯಿರಿ ಇ-ಪರಿವೇಶ್: ಲಿಂಕ್ಗೆ ಹೋಗಿ >> ಇನ್ನಷ್ಟು ತಿಳಿಯಿರಿ ಅರಣ್ಯ ನ್ಯಾಯಲಯ ಪ್ರಕರಣ ನಿರ್ವಹಣೆ ವ್ಯವಸ್ಥೆ ಲಿಂಕ್ಗೆ ಹೋಗಿ >> ಇನ್ನಷ್ಟು ತಿಳಿಯಿರಿ ಇ-ಪರಿಚಯ್ ಲಿಂಕ್ಗೆ ಹೋಗಿ >> ಇನ್ನಷ್ಟು ತಿಳಿಯಿರಿ ಇ- ಕಾರ್ಯನಿರ್ವಹಣಾ ವರದಿ ಲಿಂಕ್ಗೆ ಹೋಗಿ >> ಇನ್ನಷ್ಟು ತಿಳಿಯಿರಿ ಸರ್ಕಾರಿ ಇ-ಮಾರುಕಟ್ಟೆ ಲಿಂಕ್ಗೆ ಹೋಗಿ >> ಇನ್ನಷ್ಟು ತಿಳಿಯಿರಿ ಇ-ಆಫೀಸ್ ಲಿಂಕ್ಗೆ ಹೋಗಿ >> ಇನ್ನಷ್ಟು ತಿಳಿಯಿರಿ ಆನ್ ಲೈನ್ನಲ್ಲಿ ಮಾಹಿತಿ ಹಕ್ಕು ಅಧಿನಿಯಮದ ಮಾಹಿತಿ ವ್ಯವಸ್ಥೆ ಲಿಂಕ್ಗೆ ಹೋಗಿ >> ಇನ್ನಷ್ಟು ತಿಳಿಯಿರಿ ಮಾಹಿತಿ ಹಕ್ಕು ಅಧಿನಿಯಮದಡಿ ಮನವಿ ಮತ್ತು ಮೇಲ್ಮನವಿ ಮಾಹಿತಿ ವ್ಯವಸ್ಥೆ ಲಿಂಕ್ಗೆ ಹೋಗಿ >> ಇನ್ನಷ್ಟು ತಿಳಿಯಿರಿ ಕೆ.ಎಫ್.ಡಿ ಡ್ಯಾಶ್ಬೋರ್ಡ್ ಲಿಂಕ್ಗೆ ಹೋಗಿ >> ಇನ್ನಷ್ಟು ತಿಳಿಯಿರಿ ಬಯೋಟಿಕ್ ಲಿಂಕ್ಗೆ ಹೋಗಿ >> ಇನ್ನಷ್ಟು ತಿಳಿಯಿರಿ", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["aranyagovin"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_bangalorecustomsgovin_f9961268_01", "source_url": "https://bangalorecustoms.gov.in/", "title": "BANGALORE CUSTOMS – Guardians of National Security", "section": "Overview", "text": "The MOOWR scheme, or Manufacturing and Other Operations in Warehouse, allows manufacturers to import raw materials and capital goods without paying duty. The scheme is part of the Customs Act of 1962. The Indian Authorized Economic Operator (AEO) Programme, administered by the Central Board of Indirect Taxes and Customs (CBIC) since 2011, is an initiative aimed at bolstering the security and facilitation of the burgeoning volume of international trade goods. Only passengers who are carrying dutiable or prohibited goods are required to fill a Customs Declaration Form or use ATITHI mobile app to file declaration of dutiable items as well as currency with Indian Customs even before boarding the flight to India. The Authorised Courier has to present the export goods to the concerned officer for inspection, examination, and assessment. For certain export goods, a regular Shipping Bill, as mentioned in the Shipping Bill and Bill of Export Regulations 1991, has to be filed. Customs (Administration of Rules of Origin under Trade Agreements) Rules, 2020. Once a trade agreement is finalized, CBIC issues notifications for implementing tariff concessions and rules of origin, under section 25 of the Customs Act and section 5 of the Customs Tariff Act respectively, in order to incorporate the commitments undertaken in domestic legislation. Reporting Offenses: Your Opportunity to Make a Difference Have you come across any illegal activities related to contraband goods, customs duty evasion, or other violations concerning customs and taxation laws? Your valuable information has the potential to not only uphold law and order but also render you eligible for a substantial reward. The Bengaluru Customs Zone plays a crucial role in ensuring the enforcement of customs laws, preventing illegal trade, and facilitating legitimate international trade in the jurisdictional area vested in it. The Commissioner of Customs for Bengaluru City Customs holds authority over the entire State of Karnataka, except for the regions under the jurisdiction of the Commissioner of Customs in Mangalore. The Commissioner of Customs (Appeals) in Bengaluru plays a vital role in the administration of customs matters under the Customs Act. Here’s what you need to know about his/ her responsibilities: International Customs Day 2025 was celebrated on 15.02.2025 by this zone at Cauvery Hall, CR Building. Chief Guest- Shri.G Viswam, Director, LRDE, DRDO; Chief Commissioner – Shri.Ashish Chandan, IRS; Guest – Ms.Shuba N, Director, Wipro GE Healthcare; Guest- Shri.Rohit Dhar, COO, Emmvee Photo; retired and serving officers from the Department; other trade partners; and press representatives, were present. The vision of CBIC is to contribute to India’s socio-economic growth by implementing progressive indirect tax policies with a stakeholder-centric approach and safeguarding national interests….", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["about", "bangalorecustomsgovin", "info", "rules", "scheme"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_bangalorecustomsgovin_5b8ab132_01", "source_url": "https://bangalorecustoms.gov.in/aeo-scheme/", "title": "AEO SCHEME – BANGALORE CUSTOMS", "section": "Overview", "text": "The Indian Authorized Economic Operator (AEO) Programme, administered by the Central Board of Indirect Taxes and Customs (CBIC) since 2011, is an initiative aimed at bolstering the security and facilitation of the burgeoning volume of international trade goods. The enrolment and participation in this program by eligible stakeholders is voluntary. This program encompasses three tiers of certification for both exporters and importers: AEO T1, AEO T2, and AEO T3, with AEO T3 representing the highest level of accreditation. Currently, the program boasts nearly 5,000 AEO entities that have collaborated with Indian Customs to ensure safety and security within the supply chain. In return, these entities receive a range of benefits from Indian Customs, including expedited cargo processing and clearance, deferred duty payments, direct port delivery/entry, and mutual recognition agreements (MRAs) with other countries. The Indian AEO Programme has significantly enhanced the efficiency and cost-effectiveness of goods movement through Indian ports. To align with international best practices, CBIC has fully digitized the application filing, processing, and delivery of AEO certification. To find out more about the Indian Customs AEO program & to Self- Register for AEO certification, click on the link below: AEO Scheme Booklet", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["about", "bangalorecustomsgovin", "process", "scheme"], "language": "en"}
