{"id": "civic_wcdhrygovin_3473f8c7_01", "source_url": "https://wcdhry.gov.in/about-department/introduction/", "title": "Introduction | Women and Child Development Department, Haryana | India", "section": "Overview", "text": "Introduction The Directorate of Women and Child Development has been functioning w.e.f. 01.04.1992 vide Notification No. 79-SW I/92 dated 10th February, 1992, following its bifurcation from the Social Welfare Department. As the nodal agency for the advancement of women and children in the State, the Department is responsible for formulating policies, plans, and programmes, and for coordinating efforts of both Government and Non-Governmental Organizations working in the field of women and child development. The Directorate and its constituent organizations work in close collaboration with social organizations as well as international agencies such as UNICEF, the World Bank, UNFPA, etc., to achieve the objectives of women and child development. The Department implements various schemes and programmes for the overall development of women and children under State and Central Government initiatives, as well as with assistance from international agencies. Further, the Directorate is administratively responsible for the Haryana State Commission for Women, Haryana Women Development Corporation, and the Haryana State Social Welfare Advisory Board.", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["scheme", "wcdhrygovin"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_wcdhrygovin_a95b2893_01", "source_url": "https://wcdhry.gov.in/about-department/vision/", "title": "Vision | Women and Child Development Department, Haryana | India", "section": "Overview", "text": "Vision To facilitate the economic and social empowerment of women, enabling them to contribute as healthy, confident, and equal partners in society within an environment free from violence and discrimination. To provide children and adolescent girls with opportunities for holistic growth and development in a safe, secure, and nurturing environment.", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["wcdhrygovin"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_hryesigovin_04338753_01", "source_url": "https://hryesi.gov.in/", "title": "Homepage | Employees State Insurance Health Care | India", "section": "Overview", "text": "The country’s first multi-dimensional social security scheme for workers in the organized sector, introduced in 1952. Covers a total beneficiary population of 44 million today in whole Country. It has the country’s largest medical infrastructural facilities under one umbrella. Is the most affordable social security scheme with the lowest contribution rate for multiple health benefits. Takes care of the worker and his/her dependents from day one of entering in the insurable employment. An Act to provide for setting out the practical regime of right to information for citizens to secure access to information under the control of public authorities, in order to promote transparency and accountability in the working of every public authority, the constitution of a Central Information Commission and State Information Commissions and for matters connected therewith or incidental thereto. Whereas the Constitution of India has established democratic Republic. And whereas democracy requires an informed citizenry and transparency of information which are vital to its functioning and also to contain corruption and to hold Governments and their instrumentalities accountable to the governed. ESI Scheme is a social security scheme based on social insurance .The promulgation of Employee’s State Insurance Act, 1948 envisaged an integrated need based social insurance scheme that would protect the interest of workers in contingencies such as sickness, maternity, temporary or permanent physical disablement resulting in loss of wages or earning capacity and death due to employment injury. The Act also guarantees reasonably good medical care to workers and their immediate dependants. Under this scheme the responsibility of the State Govt. is to provide comprehensive medical care to industrial workers and their families as per agreement and provisions made under Section 58 of ESI Act 1948.", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["citizen", "hryesigovin", "info", "scheme"], "language": "en"}
