{"id": "civic_sehorenicin_2278c8f9_01", "source_url": "https://sehore.nic.in/en/citizen-services/", "title": "Website | District Sehore, Government of - Citizen Services", "section": "Overview", "text": "CITIZEN SERVICES For good governance, e-District project has been envisaged by Government of Madhya Pradesh (GoMP) as automation of workflow and internal processes of District Administration with the possibility of seamless integration of various departments for providing services to the citizens. This project is of paramount importance to the district as it would help in creating an electronic workflow system for the district administration and help in providing efficient individual department services through Common Service Centers (CSCs), Lok Sewa Kendra, MP-Online kiosks and internet, which would be the primary front end channels as envisaged in the project. eDistrict Project is being implemented under the framework of Public Service Guarantee Act. Citizens can get services through online mpedistrict portal, Login on http://mpedistrict.gov.in to get online certificate – Filter Service category wise", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["citizen", "help", "portal", "process", "sehorenicin", "service"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_sehorenicin_dd70f7f2_01", "source_url": "https://sehore.nic.in/en/generalinformation/", "title": "General Information | District Sehore, Government of Madhya Pradesh | India", "section": "Overview", "text": "General Information Sehore is 39 Km away from state capital Bhopal towards south and on Bhopal-Indore highway. Its height from the sea level is 1500 ft. to 2000 ft. It is also connected to Western Railway from Bhopal to Ratlam. District area is 6578 Km. Sehore is surrounded by Seven districts i.e. Bhopal, Raisen, Hoshangabad, Dewas, Shajapur, Rajgarh, and Harda. Sehore District extends between the parallels of Latitude 22031’to 230 40′ North and between the meridians of Longitude 76022′ and 78008′ East. The lacquer bangles of the district are a coveted adornment of the Gond , Bhiala Nad Korku tribes of the region. Bhavai, the traditional dance of these tribes is an excellent example of their artistic proclivities .In tribal area of Sehore the Bagoria dance, with its vigorous drum beating , is still performed around the Holi festival. This dance is occasion for tribal girls& boys to have run away marriage.", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["info", "sehorenicin"], "language": "en"}
{"id": "civic_sehorenicin_ab971438_01", "source_url": "https://sehore.nic.in/en/about-dic-sehore/", "title": "About DIC Sehore | District Sehore, Government of Madhya Pradesh | India", "section": "Overview", "text": "About DIC Sehore DISTRICT INFORMATICS CENTRE (NIC-Sehore) was setup in 1989 in accordance with the M.O.U. signed between NIC and Govt. of Madhya Pradesh to set up NICNET facilities in M.P.National Informatics Centre (NIC) Sehore is a premier Science & Technology institution of the Government of India, providing ICT solutions adopting best practices, integrated services and technical solutions Sehore in government departments. Since its inception NIC Sehore is providing required support services in design, development, and implementation of appropriate MIS/Databases, Training, and Electronic Communication and processing of various Departmental databases. NIC District Centre provides common ICT Infrastructure and support services to government departments with Products and Solutions designed to adopting e-Governance initiatives. NIC has taken various e-Governance activities like Samagra Samajik Surksha Monitoring , e-Uparjan, e-Scholarship, e-District (Lok Seva kendra), National Animal Disease Reporting System (NADRS), Mahatma Gandhi National Rural Employment Guarantee Act (MG-NREGA), Land Record Computerisation-Bhuabhilekh & Bhunaksha, Election MIS, Polling Party Formation for State Legislative Assembly & Parliament elections, Samadhan Online, NICNET and NKN network services, Local Area Network at Collectorate premises and Video Conferencing facility has been appreciated. The video conferencing facility extended up to five blocks and Tehsils. The services of NIC District Centre, Sehore has become an indispensable tool for the district administration and various other state and central government departments.", "category": "civic", "last_verified": "2026-10-25", "status": "verified", "quality_score": 0.92, "source_confidence": "official", "verification_method": "automated_official_source", "retrieval_tags": ["about", "info", "process", "sehorenicin", "service"], "language": "en"}
